{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers","id":297246,"title":"Werewolf 2E question for Developers, Writers, and Testers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-30T10:48:13-07:00","id":297246,"title":"Werewolf 2E question for Developers, Writers, and Testers","content":"I would like to preface this with a thank you for being a part of making my most anticipated World of Darkness book in probably ever. However, I do have a question for all of you which I assure you is not asking for spoilers or anything that may violated a NDA.<br /> <br /> I am simply curious about your thoughts on EXP growth under the 2E system especially when compared to 1E. It is hard to get a good estimate right now being that I don't have 2E source material for Werewolves, and instead must make conjectures based upon things such as Blood &amp; Smoke (or Vampire 2E).<br /> <br /> Currently, the storyteller decides to give out experience based on certain story objectives such as completing a scene, if you learned anything, roleplay etc. On average, you may wind up with 4 exp per game session. With 2E you have the conditions and beats system where 5 beats generate 1 experience and a flat growth cost as you pay the same amount per dot regardless of level.<br /> <br /> Do you find that with the current system, experience growth is reasonable? I have not switched over to the 2E system out of fear that every scene is simply going to be a player saying &quot;I make it a dramatic failure&quot; simply to collect as many beats as possible (since there can be many scenes per game session and wind up with 10-15 beats per game session once conditions are factored in.<br /> <br /> Point of fact is, I have no basis at the moment as to what a fair or average amount of beats/experience per game is considered normal and if I am going to switch over to 2E with the book release, I would love to know a baseline of sorts for what is average, what is low, and what is abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T13:21:06-07:00","id":297432,"title":"","content":"My players, never, ever went for the Dramatic Failure to reap Beats. Not even once. Wich is a source of both frustation and amusement to me when I get to bribe them with the shiny things (we use cristal beads to represent Beats to the point we don't call them Beats anymore and use a nickname &quot;<i>perlitas</i>&quot; meaning little pearls instead). &quot;<i>C'mon, you only need 2 more and everybody gets another xp</i>&quot; *grin* (we use the Group Beats option).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:57:32-07:00","id":297526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers#post297246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you find that with the current system, experience growth is reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though it is different. For me this is a good thing. The growth curve is much more oriented towards player engagement and activity levels. The more players are doing with their characters, the faster their grow; in a fashion that is more in the player's hands (thus they have the motivation to move it along) rather than me throwing around arbitrary judgements on their successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have not switched over to the 2E system out of fear that every scene is simply going to be a player saying &quot;I make it a dramatic failure&quot; simply to collect as many beats as possible (since there can be many scenes per game session and wind up with 10-15 beats per game session once conditions are factored in. </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that most Beat sources have limits on how many times they can come up. Is getting 10-15 Beats per session possible? Yes. However that's a lot of scenes. Consider:<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Should be 1 per session, but lets say 2 because it was a very active one.<br /> Automatic: 1 per session.<br /> Conditions: 1 per scene.<br /> Dramatic Failures: 1 per scene.<br /> ST award: 1 per instance.<br /> Lots of Damage: 1 per instance (not actually stated as being 1/scene in the GMCU).<br /> <br /> Unless you're running 4+ scenes, with a decent amount of combat, you're not going to see that many Beats in a session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point of fact is, I have no basis at the moment as to what a fair or average amount of beats/experience per game is considered normal and if I am going to switch over to 2E with the book release, I would love to know a baseline of sorts for what is average, what is low, and what is abuse. </div> </div> </div>4-6 seems average to me for a session with 2 scenes. 6-8 if 3 scenes. I've never had 4+ scenes in a session.<br /> <br /> But there's no such thing as abuse here. If they earned 15 beats in a Session then they earned them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T15:04:51-07:00","id":297529,"title":"","content":"Beats system is what ultimately swayed me into pro-NWoD camp, and I'm simply happy we get another 2ed game. I feel 1ed system suits OWoD more, actually, but that's my personal opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T15:15:45-07:00","id":297531,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms, you have perhaps said the most earth shattering thing to me with your statement just there and one that warrants me creating an entirely different thread to ask about so as to not derail this one. I will be posting it in the main world of darkness section. In the meantime, it is so far good to hear that the system seems balanced in terms of experience, even if I do wonder why people are not taking any of you up on the Dramatic Failure option.<br /> <br /> Spin off thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/297533-what-makes-a-scene\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-makes-a-scene</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 10-30-2014, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T18:43:00-07:00","id":297692,"title":"","content":"IIRC the dramatic failure one was per chapter, IE - game session. This is; making a failure into a dramatic one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T18:47:48-07:00","id":297693,"title":"","content":"For my part, players are earning somewhere around 3 Beats or so per game session. Some will occasionally pick up 5 if they're having a good night, but there are two factors that help that along:<br /> <br /> 1. I play with a bunch of actors.<br /> 2. I'm also somewhat generous with the &quot;good RP&quot; Beats, because I like to encourage that.<br /> <br /> Depending on the night, and how long we play, we can get in probably three or four decent scenes in a game session, so I'd say for the most part, everyone's finding some way to earn a Beat in each scene. And unlike others in this thread, I have had players deliberately opt for the Dramatic Failure just to get a Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T18:53:20-07:00","id":297694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=297693#post297693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And unlike others in this thread, I have had players deliberately opt for the Dramatic Failure just to get a Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to make characters with a dump stat in order to get at least a failure sometimes. Usually Wits for the oh so common perception rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T19:04:42-07:00","id":297698,"title":"","content":"It can be tough to get players used to the idea of intentionally screwing their character over for a benefit when they aren't used to it. When I introduced my gang to stuff like Fate or, more radically, Houses of the Blooded, it took a lot of adjustment. The latter was almost easier, since the game is explicitly about having your character ultimately betrayed and defeated in the most dramatic, operatic way possible. Once they got used to it, though, it became second nature. My advice is to, as you appear to be doing, bring it up to remind them it is an option and they'll probably get the idea. It just takes getting used to. And some people never will. I have played with Fate players who are never interested in accepting compels and that's okay. Some people aren't interested in taking on failures that aren't dictated by the dice because it undermines their fun. Different strokes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T19:24:14-07:00","id":297723,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Dramatic Failure beat, I could see it depending a lot on the Storyteller or the players previous experiences. If you have a harsh Storyteller, taking a dramatic failure can be a death sentence, and many players and Storytellers seem to come from a mindset where the game is players versus gamemaster, rather than a cooperative storytelling experience. The dramatic failures haven't come up every session but they do a fair amount, we tended to average 4 beats a game session.<br /> <br /> We played Changeling before, first edition of course, and when the GMC rules came out we decided to just go with the flat experience costs while keeping our experience the same. This led to more high dot purchases (it was played over the course of two years). Honestly, I would have seen it as a problem if we had started doing that earlier, but most of our games haven't lasted that long and been played so often.<br /> <br /> We switched to playing mortal and ghoul using GMC when the Reap the Whirlwind quickstart came out, then Blood and Smoke when that came out. I think the only really noticeable change is that you're not going to be waiting through months of sessions to get things like your Humanity from 6 to 7, or Power Stat to anything above 3. I don't see that as a problem necessarily, but I know some might, and if they tend towards long games with frequent sessions you could find yourself dealing with a high power situation when you're not ready for it. This doesn't break the game or anything, it's just something a storyteller should be aware of so they can know what stories might be appropriate for the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-30-2014, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T19:35:41-07:00","id":297726,"title":"","content":"Interesting points and it seems that anywhere from 3-5 seems to be the norm across all game lines using GMC rules for experience. I do tend to run longer games which average about 6-8 hours each 2x a month so maybe a bit more experience would be the norm simply due to game length. In all honesty, perhaps a bit more experience would do good since under the current system, you could easily drop 200 experience on a Werewolf and still not be anywhere close to PU 6+ while having anything more than average attributes. This way players get to experience some of the perks of growing in power beyond the usual raise skills first because they are cheap.<br /> <br /> Being honest, in the current 1E system, I don't believe I have ever had a single player take any power stat above 4 due to prohibitive cost versus minimum reward. Maybe now it will actually be a relevant choice (hopefully).<br /> <br /> Thanks for the response all so far by the way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T22:48:40-07:00","id":297845,"title":"","content":"Well, if the VtR 2e rules and the WtF 2e spoilers are any indication, the new Power Stats are more appealing in general. The flat costs scheme in 2e adds considerably to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:57:26-08:00","id":299885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/284946-werewolf-2e-gone-to-editing?p=293163#post293163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, those thoughts about the Dominance Gift...<br /> <br /> I've torn out the old Dominance limitations on targets, and nothing in rewriting or playtesting makes me feel like there's any reason to put it back in.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Should it be considered as &quot;Now Domination gift work normaly against the other supernatural beings&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T03:47:13-08:00","id":299897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers#post297246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you find that with the current system, experience growth is reasonable? I have not switched over to the 2E system out of fear that every scene is simply going to be a player saying &quot;I make it a dramatic failure&quot; simply to collect as many beats as possible (since there can be many scenes per game session and wind up with 10-15 beats per game session once conditions are factored in.</div> </div> </div> </div>We ran with the group beats optional rule for our playtesting because my group prefer it. Overall, if anything, advancement has felt a little slow, but that may be due to it being a playtest so players spending a lot of time feeling out the new systems etc.<br /> <br /> I have had no problems with dramatic failures; I think we've had players take them once or twice, but in general a dramatic failure is a <i>bad thing</i> for the character themselves, and sucking up as many of them as possible just for Beats is a fast ticket to Everything's Gone To Hell Town.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=297726#post297726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being honest, in the current 1E system, I don't believe I have ever had a single player take any power stat above 4 due to prohibitive cost versus minimum reward. Maybe now it will actually be a relevant choice (hopefully).</div> </div> </div> </div>The only time I ever had players go for higher Primal Urges was when we did a mini-Chronicle with an explicitly very experienced pack, and even then I think PU4 was the highest. In our regular games, PU3 was as high as a player got.<br /> <br /> The new PU is a lot better. My personal pet hate from 1e, the social penalty from Primal Urge, is gone, plus the advantages it gives are generally better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=299885#post299885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should it be considered as &quot;Now Domination gift work normaly against the other supernatural beings&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The new Dominance Gift has no targeting restrictions based on whether the target is supernatural, human or werewolf, so yes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T05:11:26-08:00","id":299919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=297694#post297694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to make characters with a dump stat in order to get at least a failure sometimes. Usually Wits for the oh so common perception rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my case, it wasn't even that. The player just decided that the scene could use a bit more chaos or bad luck, and opted for a Dramatic Failure. He was trying to do a seduction roll, and failed. He opted for the Dramatic Failure, so other characters burst into the scene as poorly as they could, and ruined the entire thing. Still, based on the further roleplaying of that scene, the seductee in question gave a clue to another PC, who was vying with the first one for her attention.<br /> <br /> All in all, it was a great scene and a lot of fun. But, as Chris says, too many of those, and things go downhill very quickly. But used sparingly, with an eye for interesting conflict, I think they work very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T08:25:38-08:00","id":300012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=299897#post299897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We ran with the group beats optional rule for our playtesting because my group prefer it. Overall, if anything, advancement has felt a little slow, but that may be due to it being a playtest so players spending a lot of time feeling out the new systems etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that particular subject, how does your group enjoy the group beats option versus the standard individual option? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=299897#post299897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only time I ever had players go for higher Primal Urges was when we did a mini-Chronicle with an explicitly very experienced pack, and even then I think PU4 was the highest. In our regular games, PU3 was as high as a player got.<br /> <br /> The new PU is a lot better. My personal pet hate from 1e, the social penalty from Primal Urge, is gone, plus the advantages it gives are generally better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this in a nutshell. My all time annoyance in Werewolf was having a social character unable to do social things. For that reason, I would be forced to intentionally keep PU at 1 and be unable to enjoy the benefits from later systems such as Aspects which require PU 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T01:25:34-08:00","id":300871,"title":"","content":"Are there something like Pack Aspirations in new edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T07:58:03-08:00","id":301119,"title":"","content":"I think that the Pack totem Aspiration functions for all members of a pack","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T08:45:36-08:00","id":301148,"title":"","content":"If now the most of gifts is on the quite the same power-level, how the charecter's progress will work? I mean, will be the real power difference between cub with PU1 and uber-elder with PU3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:32:04-08:00","id":301272,"title":"","content":"Well, the facets may all be geared as &quot;three dot powers&quot;, but all of the ones that I have seen thus far scale very powerfully with their respective renown. A non rahu with 5 purity may not have any five dot powers, but he does have five purity tied powers that all scale off of that trait, just from spoiled material, that means being able to use slaughterer to add five damage to a hit so long as you're in Gauru form, adding five mammalian predators to your pack, shutting down lights and electronics in a five block radius, and probably being able to add five strength to yourself for a scene &quot;that last one is conjecture based on what Acrozatarim's teases.&quot; So, while you may not get a huge uber power, you do get a whole bunch of powers that all scale off of your maxed out stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:14:49-08:00","id":301313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301119#post301119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Pack totem Aspiration functions for all members of a pack</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301148#post301148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If now the most of gifts is on the quite the same power-level, how the charecter's progress will work? I mean, will be the real power difference between cub with PU1 and uber-elder with PU3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts increase in power with Renown, either because they're Moon Gifts so still on a 1-5 scale, or because they're Shadow/Wolf Gifts that use Renown in dice pools or elsewhere in mechanics. The Renown link was always the case but previously high-dot powers were gated behind a Renown speed bump while now Renown is an enhancement/enabler.<br /> <br /> Primal Urge is orthogonal to Renown and Gifts, just as it was in 1e. As there, it controls trait maxima and Essence, but also now Regeneration.<br /> <br /> At PU 1, you can have up to 5 in your (Hishu) Attributes, can spend 1 Essence each turn out of a pool of 10, and regenerate 1 bashing (1 lethal with 1 Essence) per turn.<br /> At PU 10, you can have up to 10 in your (Hishu) Attributes, can spend 15 Essence each turn out of a pool of 75, and regenerate 6 bashing (6 lethal with 1 Essence) per turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T13:22:07-08:00","id":301467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301313#post301313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At PU 10, you can have up to 10 in your (Hishu) Attributes, can spend 15 Essence each turn out of a pool of 75, and regenerate 6 bashing (6 lethal with 1 Essence) per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me: do the Essence numbers by Primal Urge basically mirror the Vitae numbers by Blood Potency from VtR2e (i.e. PU5 has a pool of 15 rather than 14, PU6 has a pool of 20 rather than 15, PU7 has a pool of 25 rather than 20, PU10 has a pool of 75 rather than 100)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T14:30:46-08:00","id":301527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301467#post301467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me: do the Essence numbers by Primal Urge basically mirror the Vitae numbers by Blood Potency from VtR2e (i.e. PU5 has a pool of 15 rather than 14, PU6 has a pool of 20 rather than 15, PU7 has a pool of 25 rather than 20, PU10 has a pool of 75 rather than 100)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Vampire and Werewolf 2e both share the same scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T17:14:26-08:00","id":301579,"title":"","content":"Has there been any changes to how Uratha acquire Essense in the new edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:50:14-08:00","id":301673,"title":"","content":"From the blog we can see they get essence from Loci, and by feeding on spirits and humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:56:45-08:00","id":301676,"title":"","content":"Put another way, from the watering hole and from the prey.<br /> <br /> No McDonalds for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:57:43-08:00","id":301677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301579#post301579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any changes to how Uratha acquire Essense in the new edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, nothing new has been released on how to regain essence. I do know from past blog and dev posts that at higher levels of Primal Urge, regaining essence is going to almost certainly cause breaking points towards spirit due to the high demands required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T23:00:30-08:00","id":301840,"title":"","content":"<br /> More experienced werewolves will also have more Gifts and likely better Skills and Merits. They have the edge in versatility over their younger brethren, which sometimes counts for just as much as raw power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301313#post301313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At PU 10, you can have up to 10 in your (Hishu) Attributes, can spend 15 Essence each turn out of a pool of 75, and regenerate 6 bashing (6 lethal with 1 Essence) per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention your passive regeneration goes up by a likewise amount. At Primal Urge 10, you regenerate 6 lethal every 15 minutes! All but the most heinous of wounds will heal within half an hour. Outside of combat or other dangerous situations, a werewolf of high Primal Urge can fully heal with a short break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301677#post301677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, nothing new has been released on how to regain essence. I do know from past blog and dev posts that at higher levels of Primal Urge, regaining essence is going to almost certainly cause breaking points towards spirit due to the high demands required.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just like anything else in a werewolf's life: she has to work for it. Uratha regain Essence a variety of ways, but probably the most common will be from loci and from hunting spirits. The latter is especially thematic and also requires that werewolves act like werewolves. It doesn't necessarily lead to breaking points toward spirit\u2014but high Primal Urge werewolves have to hunt a lot more and/or bigger game than cubs. That's also fitting. Greater risk, greater reward.<br /> <br /> Everything discussed above also means it's much more difficult to push a highly experienced werewolf to her limits. When you do, look out\u2014not only does she have tremendous physical and magical capabilities, she also knows that going all-out means leaving herself more vulnerable later. So if you <i>do </i>manage to push that werewolf past the brink, she'll be desperate and extremely driven. I'd rather not be on the other side of that fight. A cornered animal, indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T00:17:34-08:00","id":301904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301676#post301676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put another way, from the watering hole and from the prey.<br /> <br /> No McDonalds for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if we call a sacred hunt on the spirit of fast food?<br /> <br /> <i>Kaylee</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Is that him? </span></span><br /> <i>Mal</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: That's the buffet table. </span></span><br /> <i>Kaylee</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Well, how can we be sure, u-unless we question it?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T06:54:25-08:00","id":302104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=301527#post301527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Vampire and Werewolf 2e both share the same scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda wonder what do you do with all that essence per turn if you can only turn on the healing once. Then it hit me werewolves will have access to stuff like Influences, and who knows why not stuff like Blast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T21:56:14-08:00","id":302977,"title":"","content":"(And this is what happens when I drink too much coffee.)<br /> <br /> <i>Shayne held her breath as she tried to stifle the anticipation within her chest. Behind her, members of the tribe yipped and danced around the bonfire as the ritual reached it's zenith. The landscape of the junkyard twisted and whirled as wicked winds worked themselves into a frenzy. The dancers forms shifted, flesh, bone, and sinew reordered themselves to give exotic outlines against the brightness of the fire. She looked at her spear and worked harden rebar against the blackened blade. Her tighten grip doing it's best to hide the anxiety within her. She looked up at the moon mother and steered herself for the trial ahead.<br /> <br /> The dancers died down as did the wind. The ritual complete, they awaited in silence, even the ever restless spirits of fire talked to themselves in hushed crackling tones. A few moments past, the moon mother's light glaring upon them all. She gritted her teeth as the second past. Did they do something wrong she wonder? Did a dancer take a misstep? Did the site location repulse their intended guest? A thousand questions ran through her mind like a herd of rabbits fleeing the hawk's shadow. She again sharpened her blade, feeling the spirit's thirst for blood.<br /> <br /> A light snap broke the stillness. She looked up to find the enormous red wolf materializing from the wreckage. He gave a quick sniff upon the wind and pawed a burnt out husk of a car. After testing it's weight, he settled on top of it, much like a king upon a throne. It's metallic shell shrieking as his bulk fell upon it. He turns his darken amber eyes upon the tribe. Shayne casts aside the rebar and sheaths her spear upon her back. She rubs her fingers together, trying to find some outlet for her nervous anticipation</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>The Firstborn eyes the site, as if looking upon a trophy that his pack has given him, then grunts. &quot;A scavenger's den, crude but understandable for our purposes.&quot; His eyes his pack again. &quot;So for what purpose has my adopted children called to me for? An enemy vexes you? A bothersome question? or perhaps some new enemy to rend apart and disassemble?&quot; Ethereal drool drops from his lips. &quot;The last sounds most appealing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye continued to fidget. An elder appeared before the great wolf, appealing and lobbying for the right to include her into the tribe. She did her best to look composed as she heard the fire continue to crack and burn behind her. Moments seem to turn into hours before she felt those amber eyes burn into hers. She nodded and approached, her arms outstretched, her head bowed as she did.<br /> <br /> She felt the Firstborn nostrils upon her, taking in her scent. &quot;Quiet, Athletic, Young, like a fresh pup.&quot; He pauses. &quot;No scent of victory, no scent of deeds.&quot;<br /> <br /> She gritted her teeth, panicked thoughts started to race within the confines of her mind. &quot;Pack leader,&quot; she said in a trembling voice. &quot;I brought down a pain spirit which troubled the mortal world, I gave the killing blow and salted the area so no of it's tainted essence could grow.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn chuckled. &quot;Indeed, you have and you would make a great Suthar Anzuth or Iminir but such a deed does not place you well in my pack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye felt her fists curl into balls, her Rage rising. She had deed! She had victories! By what reason and right was Sagrim-Ur judging her on? She opened her mouth to give an angry retort when a sudden crash pierced the conversation. The sound of rude almost musical notes that traveled behind it added insult to injury. Both she and the wolf god turned to the source, a small human figure climbed it's self back upon the railing. A snarling rang up from the tribe and each member gave an inhuman predatory look upon the intruding human. They all heard the word that followed. A base and human word. Muffled a bit by it's distance but still keeping it's bite.<br /> <br /> &quot;FUCK!&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <i>She heard a snarl behind her, Sagrim-Ur's pinned back, his mouth turned into a misshapen grin. &quot;Human&quot; he whispered and gave a howl that cracked the sky. The tribe spurred into motion, the vanguards already working them way up the railing, their Dalu forms swinging up the metal work like great apes. Shanye's body tightened as she ran in Urhan only to feel a strong bite pull her back. She turned and growled only to face Sagirm-Ur's toothy grin.<br /> <br /> &quot;Patience young one, we wait for now.&quot;<br /> <br /> Huffing in irritation and baring her teeth, she sat next to the great wolf. Waiting for the others to return. Rage began to build. She was being denied the hunt! She was being denied her birthright! By what reason did this spirit to deny the very urge that writhed within her blood and bones? She gave dull growl to show her displeasure. Red Wolf gave no notice, his eyes and ears upon the water tower, waiting for his adopted children to return.<br /> <br /> And slowly return they did. One by one, they climbed back down. Mild disappointment fell from a few faces but others gave excited yips, yelps, and words. They got to run, they got briefly got to hunt. She noted and sulked. Two of their number came before Red Wolf. One wiping egg off his face while another, blood. They gave excited chatter among themselves as they proceed to prostrate. He eyed them both curiously. &quot;I'm assuming that the quarry gone to ground? Or perhaps he was claimed by a spirit of eggs that my pack then scrambled?&quot;<br /> <br /> The blood faced one spoke first. &quot;Elder, the quarry is a mortal man. I tasted no spirit among his blood, flesh, nor scent. However, I've heard local nearby spirits chatter. They know his face, they've been to his home. They gossip to themselves that he is an observer, an outsider who plans on publishing his travels.&quot; He looks upon the Firstborn, teeth bared. &quot;We will tear out this cancer before it spreads.&quot;<br /> <br /> A long moment past, the once raging bonfire now a series of embers crackling against the dark of the night. Shanye continued to remain silent, doing her best to contain her annoyance as her role this night was placed into a more passive one. Sagrim-Ur gave a series of thumps with his paw that rang out upon the metallic husk of the car. He stopped, and all the tribe turned toward him, snarling and grinning at the forgone reply.<br /> <br /> &quot;No.'&quot;<br /> <br /> A look of puzzlement and confusion flash upon the faces of the tribe, their demeanor shifting from one of confidence and twitching claws to one of hesitance and discord. War forms shifted shifted back into passive ones. Confusion started to give way to Rage and Shayne's was starting to boil over like an ill kept cooking pot. Words began to frayed into raw emotion and she was just about at her limit when the egg faced one spoke up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pack master! My pack owns the territory of whi-&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye blinked. Within the jaws of the Firstborn lay the neck of the speaker. He gave a pitiful yelp, like a dog who's leg was caught in a trap. Red Wolf kept that posed for a second or two before spitting the offending Uratha out. He glared at the rest of his tribe.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are my adopted children but you are still my children. While you are my child, you are in my pack.&quot; He snarled. &quot;And while you are in my pack. YOU WILL FOLLOW MY ORDERS!&quot; He turned toward Shanye. &quot;Is this clear?&quot;<br /> <br /> A light mummer of acknowledgments and growls rang out from the crowd. Shanye gulped and gave hers.<br /> <br /> The wolf god turned toward his castigate. &quot;Take the spirits, go to this mortals home. Burn all traces of his life. Leave his tools.&quot;<br /> <br /> He turned toward Shanye. &quot;Follow him, Watch this mortal. If he takes his tools, hunt him down. When you have him trapped, call to me. Consider this your trial.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye got up and trailed after the waiting Uratha, his bite marks already healing. Shanye gritted her teeth and balled her hands then relaxed. She got her trial, she got Red Wolf's approval. All that was needed was to hunt down this damn mortal. She licked her lips. How hard could that be?<br /> <br /> ************************************************** ************************************************** **************************************************<br /> <br /> Shanye cursed. It was three weeks into this trial and this was the third time her quarry slipped her grasp. She gave a sharp kicked to the bedding, sending a sizable crack up it's frame.<br /> <br /> &quot;He's clever&quot; said one of her improvised pack mates. &quot;I'll give him that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye gave a growl. &quot;We had him. We choked off his exits and tracked him down here. How in the everlasting holy fuck did he get away this time?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you sure this is a mortal? Not a mage or shaman?&quot; said one of another as he probed the stacks of empty canned food.<br /> <br /> Another one sipped on a plastic bottle filled with dark yellow liquid. &quot;He's stressed, lack of sleep most likely. Still mortal and most likely not a wizard.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What makes you say that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He wouldn't be pissing in bottles for one thing. Would've tasted it in his blood and scent for another.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye ignored the banter as she eyes a series of discarded notebooks. She began to flip through them. Her curiosity piking. She pointed out the general ledger the first part of the notebook, diagrams and graphs on the second, and a hierarchy chart in the last.<br /> <br /> &quot;Someone's been busy.&quot; she muttered. A tiny bit of respect for her prey burrowing out of the contempt of her mind. She looked over the first section. The contacts were noted in simple dots, no names, no symbols, no identifying markers but below them were items, indicators of trade. She eyed the items. A fistful seeds, a few burnt out CDs, Tree bark thriced struck by skyfire. As she read, her mind began to open, she began to understand.<br /> <br /> &quot;</i><i>Chiminage</i><i>. He's trading with </i><i>chiminage</i><i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Her pack mates turned towards her, eyes confused.<br /> <br /> &quot;No wonder we can't ever seem to pin this asshole down! He's trading with spirits! They're covering his ass!&quot;<br /> <br /> Movement within the room halted. The rustling of pages echoed as she frantically flipped to the charts. She pointed at names underlined. &quot;Marcus, Liquine, Tonya, Default...&quot; she stopped at hers, underlined in red. Rage crept within her but so did another feeling, one she hadn't felt for a long while. It's icy sensation moved along her spine as the Rage grew within her. She dropped the book as she slammed her fist into the metal wall twice. Rage begin to drain leaving the cold, hard feeling in her guts. Her mind took a moment to remember what it was. It was fear. She was feeling fear.<br /> <br /> &quot;He knows about us. I don't know how he got the information or who he bribed but he knows.&quot;<br /> <br /> She took a moment to again compose herself and flipped over to last section. Details of the tribe were laid before her. The elders, the novices, etc, etc, and above it all was an outline of Red Wolf. She began to trace all of the outlines. &quot;This isn't true. This certainly is. Here, here, and here...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I trust the hunt is going well.&quot;<br /> <br /> She looked up to spy a muscular figure clad the local uniform, complete with mop and bucket. His eyes flashed red as he scanned at the room, demeanor as if he was an audience member in art gallery, looking over an exhibit. &quot;Bit spartan for my liking but it would do in a pinch.&quot; he muttered to himself.<br /> <br /> She bowed her head, the best display of respect that she could give on short notice. &quot;Elder, we just got done tracking him down here but he slipped the net via one of those damned doorways. We've managed to find some interesting notes however.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn licked his lips. &quot;Do tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> She handed him the ragged notebook. &quot;From the first section, we've seen that he's been trading with spirits to remain in the Shadow long term. Hence his ability to survive long term in it. He doesn't seem to be able to use essence but understands the value of </i><i>chiminage</i><i> in transactions.&quot; She spied the buckets of human waste in the corner. &quot;I believe he's using his naturally produced waste to trade for food. It would make good fertilizer that the plant choir would find acceptable.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn nodded. &quot;Crude but clever. What else?&quot; as he flipped through the notebook.<br /> <br /> &quot;He keeps his contacts secret, apparently a trait from his journalistic days, but his records are plain to see. He trades with the data choir, the plant choir, and the city choir.&quot;<br /> <br /> The false janitor cocked an eyebrow. &quot;Meaning...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If we shake down or bribe these choirs, we can find these spirits and cut them out.<br /> <br /> The janitor gave an approving smirk. A toothy smile crept across his face. &quot;What else?&quot;<br /> <br /> She panted, trying to recall the data that she just read. Her brain reeled as wheels started to turn. &quot;He's done his homework on us. He knows our people, he knows our pack, he knows our tribe...&quot; She looked up at the janitor. &quot;He knows our names elder, he knows you.&quot;<br /> <br /> To her shock, he simply nodded. &quot;How are you plugging the holes in which he travels?&quot;<br /> <br /> She stammered a bit, the Firstborn's indifference rattling her nerves, and pulled out a map &quot;We..We've mapped most of them out. He seems to track here and here. I think we've gotten most of them mapped. Less he starts finding new ones to open.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn casually opened the document, flipping through to the relationship graphs and tables. He gave a smirk at the end and gave it back to Shayne. &quot;Continue the hunt.&quot;<br /> <br /> She looked up on the Firstborn, her weary expression showing upon her face. &quot;As you wish elder.&quot; She gave a puzzled look. &quot;Do you always follow our trials so closely?&quot;<br /> <br /> The reply was instant and flat. &quot;No.&quot;<br /> <br /> The pack resumed it's pillage of the lair as the janitor left the hide out, mopping the floor as he went. She heard a just audio sigh outside the door. &quot;He would have made a good Uratha...&quot;<br /> <br /> ************************************************** ************************************************** **************************************************<br /> <br /> Shanye threw her spear and was rewarded with a scream of agony. The spirit flew true and it manage to snag the mortal's left thigh. He hobbled towards he door, his spoon-keys fumbling in hand. She fell four legs as she shifted. This was the fifth time they've burned him out and she was dead certain to make it the last. With a sudden turn, he threw a glass drinking jar filled with a green substance at her. It connected and she fell as a serpent spirit coiled around her. She gave a mix of wolfish yip and a human scream as it coiled around her, locking her legs. Her prey was so close. So damn close that she could smell his blood, his flesh, his fear.<br /> <br /> With a quick motion, she subdued the serpent and broke it's neck before looking up. The door was shutting and with a quick throw, she lodge the serpents body against it, preventing it from shutting. She quickly grabbed her spear and, with panting breath, race after the mortal.<br /> <br /> She felt the cool night air against her chest as followed the blood trail out of the gas station, her Rage growing to match her body. There were no doors in this area of the city to hide in, no escape. She continued to hungry follow the blood. Her form growing as large as a car as it crashed into the tower's lobby. Had she been paying attention, she would've caught a sweet scent in the air, somewhat...pure but her mind simply caught the closing of the stair door and rush in after it.<br /> <br /> She barged into the stairway, her Rage overcoming her, shifting into her war form. She heard her prey slinging insult at delusions, asking prayers to figures that didn't exist. As she climbed up the stairs, her Rage...subsided. Something in the air took the edge off her nerves. More control. She shook her head briefly. Guru always led to Rage didn't it? Rage was Guru and Guru was Rage. This shouldn't be happening. Why is this...<br /> <br /> The desire to hunt kicked back in as she heard her prey barge out the door. She continued upwards, and busted the door off it's hinges with a massive shove. She spied him a few feet away, writing his name in the tower with his blood.<br /> <br /> Trembling, she drew here spear. She called out Red Wolf's name under her breath as she stood beside him and leveled it at the throat of his prone form. His eyes rapidly blinking, his body torn and ragged. His clothes in not much better shape. His tools crude, and esoteric. His words babbling about fever dreams before slipping into sleep. She gave a series of taps to keep him awake. Her features soften. He so pitiful when he's not such a major pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> Behind her, her pack mates assembled, coming to see the being which until recently, vexed them all greatly. They huddled around the babbling prone figure, giving curious looks and sideways glances. They began to talk among themselves.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is this the mortal which outran us for so long? Doesn't look like much now.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How did he know so much about the damn city? He made his damn home everywhere were we couldn't see!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Just throw him off the building or slice his throat. Just get it over with, it's damn cold up here without any pants.&quot;<br /> <br /> They hushed up as Sagrim-Ur materialized and eyed the prone figure. The man's head seem to lift for a second. &quot;Sagrim...?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn moved closer, tail giving slight wags as he proceeds to take in the babbling man's scent. &quot;Quite the chase, little one. Breaking tenets you do not know, Stumbling around into places your kind should have no knowledge from. Quite clever I must admit&quot; Shayne remains in position, frozen as the Firstborn examines her prey. </i><br /> <br /> <i>He gives another sniff and cocks his head to the side. A puzzled look. &quot;Curious, I smelt a mortal before this hunt began and now I smell a umma.&quot; Shanye twists her spear. She's heard the stories. Red Wolf glares at him above his head. &quot;Where have you been little umma? What lands have you just got back from traveling&quot;. He gives a quick sniff behind his ears, pausing as he seems to catch something he does not expect. She again hears a whisper. &quot;Pangaea?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn gives a growl as he raises his head towards the rest of his tribe. The intention clear, they huddle out, trekking down the stairway. Shanye takes the spear off the throat but sits down beside them. The gentle cool night air matching their breathing. </i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Tell me everything umma.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>It was as if a dam of information had been breached. The human started from his early days. Of journalism, told of how he discovered the Shadow. Of his host and spoon keys. Of his mysterious guest and his demented travels. He told of the secret areas between material and Shadow. Of the Azlu nest on Baker street and the nest of rats working their way through Mission District. He told of his narrow escapes and sleepless nights. Of his desire for knowledge of the city. The way it moved, beat, worked, and thrived. He told of his secret doors and somber moments. He told of his attraction to Shanye (of which she blushed) and his network of spirits. He told of which were working to make war on the forsaken and which were friends. Lastly, he spoke of his fever dreams and honey suckled paradise. He told of a watchtower and of names and then, after all that, he told of their tribe.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn looked upon Shayne, paw pressing down upon the babbling figure, asked &quot;What is our bane? Dear umma, what is our creed?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>The reply was sharp and instant. &quot;Honor your territory in all things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shayne glanced at both, for the first time, for a long time, her mind was quiet.<br /> <br /> At last did the new umma's voice started to wither, started to fall. Sagrim-Ur's jaws went tight off and on through out the night to prod the umma's to wakefulness but even now that seem to be growing ineffective. The voice was barely above a whisper before his story finally ended and went limp.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn looked at the limp umma and took him up as a wolf takes a pup by the scruff. He beckoned Shanye to follow which she did dutifully. They took the secret passageways through the Shadow, a cut here, a trip there. They dodge angry street cars and tyrannical signs here decay and crack spirits there, of business and hope in one door, of birds and trees in another. They took in the city and the city took them in. It was as Helios was starting to rise did they finally reach the movie studio. Shanye looked at him tenderly as the Firstborn dropped him out of the Shadow, on to the material floor. They then scampered out of the way, less the Magi take greater interest.<br /> <br /> They stopped upon a broken half pipe, Helios well risen in the sky. That is when Shayne finally spoke.<br /> <br /> &quot;You planned this all along.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Firstborn gave a playful smile. &quot;I did no such thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye cocked an eyebrow at the massive wolf. &quot;Really? The prey that you send me on just so happens to have three years of experience</i> <i>in the Shadow prior</i> <i>and worked as a journalist before that and thus giving him enormous amounts of incredible</i> <i>use as we are hunting him and you expect me to believe that.<br /> <br /> The Firstborn gave a playful chuckle. &quot;Well, I may have some part to play in it but certainly not him learning about us nor him becoming umma. While you were hunting him, I was hunting as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye gave an annoyed huff. &quot;And what was that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sagirm-Ur looked out the horizon. &quot;Too much fighting, so many petty power struggles. Everyone turning on each other and their focus towards outer threats lingers and festers. Weakness should not be cuddle, this is true but our enemies are many, our nightmares organized. Does anyone know what the spider bitches were doing before this? Where the rats were keeping their nests? What choirs were throwing their allegiance</i> <i>for those three bastard mongrel tribes instead of us.&quot; He turned toward Shanye. &quot;Even my tribe forgets it's creed at times and must be shown what they pledge to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> A long moment passed between them, spirit gulls cooed and cawed.<br /> <br /> &quot;And perhaps some inking where the umma get their damnable powers.&quot; He said. &quot;It quite vexing.&quot;<br /> <br /> He turned toward Shanye. &quot;Gather the tribe, tell them to hunt. You're targets are many, and the limits of my patience thin. We will route these threats, Farsil Luhal, we will route them all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shanye bowed, and scampered off to the tribe. As she did, she finally understood. Honor your territory in all things. She finally understood. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 11-05-2014, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T22:36:57-08:00","id":303002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=302104#post302104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda wonder what do you do with all that essence per turn if you can only turn on the healing once. Then it hit me werewolves will have access to stuff like Influences, and who knows why not stuff like Blast?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that different than the situation with 1st edition Changelings. Outside of pumping very specific dice rolls (usually based off Kith &amp; Seeming), there aren't very many meaningful ways to spend 15 Glamour in one turn. That said, I wouldn't be shocked if there are Essence dumps for Werewolves besides Influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T03:30:19-08:00","id":303167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=302104#post302104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda wonder what do you do with all that essence per turn if you can only turn on the healing once. Then it hit me werewolves will have access to stuff like Influences, and who knows why not stuff like Blast?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can activate more Facets in one go with a higher Essence/turn. Many Facets are reflexive these days, particularly combat enhancements, so the Essence/turn is the limiter on how rapidly you can fire them up during a combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T05:11:25-08:00","id":303208,"title":"","content":"Can I ask also about new Streight Gifts? Which concept is planned for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T08:57:26-08:00","id":303337,"title":"","content":"*Strength gifts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T09:17:45-08:00","id":303348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303208#post303208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I ask also about new Streight Gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can use them in play, if I'm officially bi? Maybe developers could help with ruling? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T09:59:59-08:00","id":303367,"title":"","content":"Strength gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T12:16:58-08:00","id":303582,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of the Strength Gifts. Getting to Strength 9 in Gauru at character creation is fun! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T12:21:42-08:00","id":303598,"title":"","content":"I like the passive bonus gifts. Though I guess it could get very powerful using faceted gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:17:41-08:00","id":303685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303167#post303167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can activate more Facets in one go with a higher Essence/turn. Many Facets are reflexive these days, particularly combat enhancements, so the Essence/turn is the limiter on how rapidly you can fire them up during a combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me very, very happy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:38:29-08:00","id":303700,"title":"","content":"The Strength Gifts are pretty savage. They enhance the werewolf's already impressive physical capabilities and make her into an engine of carnage.<br /> <br /> 2E werewolves are all scary as hell in a fight, even if they aren't very specialized. The ones who do specialize are terrifying monsters with few peers in battle. Then you also have their pack to deal with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:52:11-08:00","id":303709,"title":"","content":"So... not really a hunter anymore (surgical killing), but more of a bestial killing machine (ala cWOD). Makes me a sad panda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:01:41-08:00","id":303711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303709#post303709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... not really a hunter anymore (surgical killing), but more of a bestial killing machine (ala cWOD). Makes me a sad panda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on what you're hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:01:42-08:00","id":303712,"title":"","content":"Surgical killing comes from other gifts, like the nature, technology, and auspice ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:04:22-08:00","id":303714,"title":"","content":"And yet you are a mostly unstoppable tank killer now (unless that has somehow changed since the spoilers, which I doubt). Still a sad panda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:15:10-08:00","id":303719,"title":"","content":"If you want to you can probably build an unstoppable tank as a character, but from what we've seen it doesn't look like that's the standard werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:35:15-08:00","id":303749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303709#post303709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... not really a hunter anymore (surgical killing), but more of a bestial killing machine (ala cWOD). Makes me a sad panda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how an enhancement of already impressive physical abilities makes you less of a hunter. The Strength Gifts enhance various aspects of a werewolf's strength, but in a way that makes them more efficient hunters\u2014including the killing part. I really don't see why all of a sudden this is disappointing rather than just another way Gifts make you better hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:38:52-08:00","id":303750,"title":"","content":"I'm not really seeing the problem. In 1st ed you were just as capable of &quot;killing a tank&quot; with the just two Strength Gifts. Iron Rending plus Savage Might plus Gauru and BAM! There you go. Heck, with Legendary Arm, you could THROW the damn thing. Not very subtle or &quot;surgical&quot; if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T14:50:05-08:00","id":303759,"title":"","content":"I agree with the other commenters, if you want to be a &quot;surgical killer&quot;, then just eschew Strength Gifts and take Gifts that fall more in line with your concept of a &quot;surgical killer&quot;. I want to note something though, some of the Firstborns, like Fenris-Ur, were not known for their subtle hunting skills. Fenris was accused by his brothers and sisters for using overwhelming force when taking down prey, thus pretty much destroying the quarry in the process. All I am saying is there are a number of different ways to hunt, there is no need to shoe horn players into one method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T16:50:07-08:00","id":303866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303714#post303714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you are a mostly unstoppable tank killer now (unless that has somehow changed since the spoilers, which I doubt). Still a sad panda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You're harder to kill than in 1e. But, that's still framed through being a hunter. Being a bestial killing machine is required, because...<br /> <br /> Okay. Humans think on the scale of humans. Fuckin... great white sharks? They're complete bastard psychos, real bestial killing machines. But they need to be. Same for the Uratha. They don't have all this ability because they're already an apex predator and just get to lord it over us more. Instead, they have all of this power because they <i>need</i> it to hunt their prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:09:33-08:00","id":303901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303866#post303866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. You're harder to kill than in 1e. But, that's still framed through being a hunter. Being a bestial killing machine is required, because...<br /> <br /> Okay. Humans think on the scale of humans. Fuckin... great white sharks? They're complete bastard psychos, real bestial killing machines. But they need to be. Same for the Uratha. They don't have all this ability because they're already an apex predator and just get to lord it over us more. Instead, they have all of this power because they <i>need</i> it to hunt their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I am sensing that the difficulty scale of enemies has been significantly increased which is not a bad thing. In 1e, I have quite a few times used a PU3 werewolf and soloed a Greater Jaggling. True, it wasn't exactly a combat specced Jaggling, but still...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:39:17-08:00","id":303928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303901#post303901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I am sensing that the difficulty scale of enemies has been significantly increased which is not a bad thing. In 1e, I have quite a few times used a PU3 werewolf and soloed a Greater Jaggling. True, it wasn't exactly a combat specced Jaggling, but still...</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at like this: the focus is now on the hunt in its myriad forms. Not just any hunt, but <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. <i>The </i>Hunt. And the prey is some of the most dangerous on Earth. Spirits. Azlu. Beshilu. Claimed. Humans. Any of which can pose a variety of threats. You're not just hunting rats. You're hunting ancient, cunning rat monsters who thrive in dark, filth-ridden places. They gnaw at the border between worlds and let through spirits of pestilence and decay. Their magic makes them difficult to run down and harder still to wipe out. Their greatest warriors are no Uratha, but fighting a Rokhan with feculent claws amid a swarm of rats, gnawing and biting at your eyes and nose while a spirit of excrement tries to drown you in offal.... well, it's no picnic. The Uratha can no longer let such monstrosities go free than they can not shapeshift. They are hunters of monsters. They must be equally monstrous.<br /> <br /> It's a supernatural ecosystem but behaves like a natural one in that respect. Predators must be up to the task of tackling their prey. Weak ones fail. Werewolves are as strong as they are because the race wouldn't last a year otherwise. And the cycle reinforces itself, because werewolf prey must be strong in turn. It's a supernatural world red in tooth and claw. Terrible things lurk in the night, preying on flesh, blood, souls, even the very essence of the world. The wolf must hunt them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 11-06-2014, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T04:20:50-08:00","id":304403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303714#post303714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you are a mostly unstoppable tank killer now (unless that has somehow changed since the spoilers, which I doubt). Still a sad panda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Tymeaus,<br /> <br /> Are you referring to my comments a while back about being able to create a Rahu that can take tank rounds and survive? I think people may have leapt to conclusions that it means said Rahu can also shred tanks, but at the time I was largely trying to illustrate the <i>potential</i> resilience of a combat-specced Full Moon.<br /> <br /> Referencing the Facets that have since been spoiled, I was making that assertion based on the notion of a Stamina 5 Rahu with Purity 5 and Glory 5 in Gauru form - a Rahu with Purity 5 has 5 additional health levels, Glory 5 allows them to use the Rage Facet Berserker's Might to spend Essence and reduce the incoming damage by 5, and I assumed an average roll on Crimson Spasm (the 5th dot Full Moon Gift) with the results heavily invested into bonus Stamina to further increase the Rahu's health level total for as long as the character's Essence supply can hold out. The idea here is to get total health levels above the incoming damage from the tank shell in order for there to be no wrap-around into Aggravated damage, so that Gauru regeneration can then clear out the Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, a Glory 5 Purity 5 Rahu is intentionally a pretty terrifying combatant, given that's pretty much an 'end-game' level of those two Renowns.<br /> <br /> So let's take an actual look at how various types of werewolf might try and take on a tank... (There will be a following post while I mull this over <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T05:03:49-08:00","id":304453,"title":"","content":"Use that one Facet that makes technological items fall apart, eat the soldiers suddenly deprived of their metal shell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T05:05:47-08:00","id":304456,"title":"","content":"So, how might different werewolves attempt to crack the problem of a tank? This is... a not entirely serious post, given we're talking about hunting a <i>tank</i>.<br /> <br /> Let's make some assumptions first.<br /> - The tank and its crew are prey and need to be hunted. The whys and wherefores aren't essential, but maybe the crew are cultists and the tank is potentially going to be an anchor for a horrible spirit when it crosses the Gauntlet.<br /> - The tank and crew are an active combatant but run through the usual cycle of necessary refuelling, repair etc; it's not a magic tank that never needs to stop and the crew are regular humans.<br /> - If the crew are affected by Lunacy, they go into the 'oh god kill it' mode rather than any of the other Lunacy Conditions. Out of their tank, they have small arms to defend themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Rahu</b><br /> You have the greatest capacity to actually go head-to-head with a tank, in terms of taking hits, but it <i>could</i> go horribly, horribly wrong even if you're the aforementioned Stamina 5 Glory 5 Purity 5 juggernaut - as soon as the tank rolls well enough with enough successes to wrap into Aggravated, you're in a downward spiral. Don't engage the tank in open combat if possible; use terrain (an urban environment are ideal) and get right up to it. Depending on your Facets and how much Durability/Structure a tank has (since I dunno off-hand), you may be able to tear through the armour but this may be a losing proposition; you <i>might</i> be able to hit high enough Strength to just flip the damn thing over but, again, I don't know how much tanks actually weigh or how much Strength would be needed. You're best off bringing an actual anti-tank explosive to slap on it, then going in through the breach. If you don't have anything like that, I'd suggest trying to muster enough physical force to wreck the tracks etc then just wait by the tank until the crew eventually have to come out.<br /> <br /> <b>Cahalith</b><br /> Go after the tank crew in their dreams whenever they sleep. Wear them down, night by night. Eventually they'll make a mistake, and then they'll hear your howl, and know they're doomed.<br /> <br /> <b>Elodoth</b><br /> Who knows how you'll catch them in your web? Maybe you'll pull some strings and the tank will be called in for maintenance, letting you pick the crew off at your leisure. Could be that some insurgents/rebels/terrorists will attack the tank and take it out for you. Maybe you'll just watch the crew when they're off-duty, learning their weaknesses then bringing each to a fitting end involving their worst vices and flaws. Maybe one of them will meet a cute boy/girl who persuades them to show them that awesome tank then, suddenly, when they turn roundit's <i>you</i>. Maybe you ward the vehicle park around their tank so that, when you attack, they just can't find their way through the maze of vehicles to the armoured safety of the thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Ithaeur</b><br /> The tank is now possessed by a spirit-ally of yours. Alternatively, it drives into a big hole that your Elemental Influences gouge up in front of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Irraka</b><br /> When one crewman gets out of the tank to have a piss, he never comes back. When they bed down in the apparent safety of the army encampment, you drag one away into the darkness. When they finally seal themselves into it in a fit of absolute terror, you somehow - <i>somehow</i> - are in there already, waiting for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talon</b><br /> You're a soldier, the tank is an objective. It's tougher than an Uratha, can be quite fast, and hits hard, but there are lots of tools designed for taking one out - landmines, AT explosives, etc - and if push comes to shove you, like the Rahu, may be strong enough to rip chunks off the thing. You just need to be careful about getting to it. Also, come in a group with other Blood Talons; one might not be able to tank-tip, but several of you can surely do it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadow</b><br /> A spirit uses its Influences and drinks away the tank's petrol, leaving it stranded and easy prey. Then you call up a blazing pyre underneath it. The prey get out or they cook. If they cook, you rip their ghosts apart just to make sure.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter in Darkness</b><br /> If they go near wilderness, you trap them amidst a knotted tangle of roads and paths that never let them out of that wood again; when they get tired and get out of the tank, you pounce. If you're nowhere near a wood, maybe you just call up a massive eruption of vines and trees underneath and around the tank. Of course, if you've mastered the Gift of Warding then you can just sink your claws into the symbolic nature of the locked access ports on the tank and flick them open with a little bit of will, leaving the prey inside suddenly vulnerable to fang and talon.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Master</b><br /> They're <i>humans</i>. In a <i>tank</i>. They're dead meat. You have two Gifts that are filled with ways to fuck a tank up, this really is no contest. There's a reason humans are your favoured prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords</b><br /> Maybe a sudden storm fills the river and rips the bridge out from under the tank as it crosses. Maybe a dense fog covers the area and you easily sneak up to it under cover, or the weather turns freezing or baking and eventually forces the prey out of their little metal shell. Hilariously, if you manage to get embroiled in a battle with several tanks, you may be able to get another one to shoot the tank that's your actual prey. If you can get to the crew outside of a combat situation, of course, you can probably get them to hand the tank over anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T05:25:15-08:00","id":304462,"title":"","content":"May be it will be more useful to speak not about &quot;how can/can't Uratha destroy tank&quot; (couse powerful fight-orientated werewolf actually could do this in 1e too) but about the other abilities? I mean, which Gifts/Facets can be used for example, for detective-work?<br /> P.S. But for this is not a problem. i mean, I like fighting in games, I like old good ultraviolence, and I like crossover - so, for me werewolf must be as strong as vampires. I don't want to play werewolf if I know that she will suck vampires'... hm-m.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T05:26:34-08:00","id":304464,"title":"","content":"Have I told you I love you Chris? Awesome ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T07:40:25-08:00","id":304556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=303749#post303749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fail to see how an enhancement of already impressive physical abilities makes you less of a hunter. The Strength Gifts enhance various aspects of a werewolf's strength, but in a way that makes them more efficient hunters\u2014including the killing part. I really don't see why all of a sudden this is disappointing rather than just another way Gifts make you better hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not &quot;all of a sudden.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I am unhappy with many of the changes to Werewolf from 1st Edition to 2nd Edition. There are some interesting ideas, to be sure, but you have taken a Hunter (from 1st Edition) and buffed them to the Combat Levels of Apocalypse (in my opinion, in 2nd - Can reliably stand against tanks? Really? Lame...). He is really not a Hunter any more, in my opinion, but something else (not sure how to explain that, really). I am probably one of the few who did not see any need to change most of the werewolf condition. The changes to Forms and Gifts are just bad, in my opinion. But then, I know I am in the minority here, so... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Any ways - You have hit on things that many people want, so keep up the good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T07:47:38-08:00","id":304558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304403#post304403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hi Tymeaus,<br /> <br /> Are you referring to my comments a while back about being able to create a Rahu that can take tank rounds and survive? I think people may have leapt to conclusions that it means said Rahu can also shred tanks, but at the time I was largely trying to illustrate the <i>potential</i> resilience of a combat-specced Full Moon.<br /> <br /> Referencing the Facets that have since been spoiled, I was making that assertion based on the notion of a Stamina 5 Rahu with Purity 5 and Glory 5 in Gauru form - a Rahu with Purity 5 has 5 additional health levels, Glory 5 allows them to use the Rage Facet Berserker's Might to spend Essence and reduce the incoming damage by 5, and I assumed an average roll on Crimson Spasm (the 5th dot Full Moon Gift) with the results heavily invested into bonus Stamina to further increase the Rahu's health level total for as long as the character's Essence supply can hold out. The idea here is to get total health levels above the incoming damage from the tank shell in order for there to be no wrap-around into Aggravated damage, so that Gauru regeneration can then clear out the Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, a Glory 5 Purity 5 Rahu is intentionally a pretty terrifying combatant, given that's pretty much an 'end-game' level of those two Renowns.<br /> <br /> So let's take an actual look at how various types of werewolf might try and take on a tank... (There will be a following post while I mull this over <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>That is part of it, perhaps, but the reality is that I think that Gifts and Forms needed no boost at all (though <i><b>maybe </b></i>PU needed something, though I am not even sure about that, to be honest)... and that informs most of my dislike for how 2nd Edition is developing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T07:58:23-08:00","id":304580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304456#post304456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how might different werewolves attempt to crack the problem of a tank? This is... a not entirely serious post, given we're talking about hunting a <i>tank</i>.<br /> <br /> Let's make some assumptions first.<br /> - The tank and its crew are prey and need to be hunted. The whys and wherefores aren't essential, but maybe the crew are cultists and the tank is potentially going to be an anchor for a horrible spirit when it crosses the Gauntlet.<br /> - The tank and crew are an active combatant but run through the usual cycle of necessary refuelling, repair etc; it's not a magic tank that never needs to stop and the crew are regular humans.<br /> - If the crew are affected by Lunacy, they go into the 'oh god kill it' mode rather than any of the other Lunacy Conditions. Out of their tank, they have small arms to defend themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Rahu</b><br /> You have the greatest capacity to actually go head-to-head with a tank, in terms of taking hits, but it <i>could</i> go horribly, horribly wrong even if you're the aforementioned Stamina 5 Glory 5 Purity 5 juggernaut - as soon as the tank rolls well enough with enough successes to wrap into Aggravated, you're in a downward spiral. Don't engage the tank in open combat if possible; use terrain (an urban environment are ideal) and get right up to it. Depending on your Facets and how much Durability/Structure a tank has (since I dunno off-hand), you may be able to tear through the armour but this may be a losing proposition; you <i>might</i> be able to hit high enough Strength to just flip the damn thing over but, again, I don't know how much tanks actually weigh or how much Strength would be needed. You're best off bringing an actual anti-tank explosive to slap on it, then going in through the breach. If you don't have anything like that, I'd suggest trying to muster enough physical force to wreck the tracks etc then just wait by the tank until the crew eventually have to come out.<br /> <br /> <b>Cahalith</b><br /> Go after the tank crew in their dreams whenever they sleep. Wear them down, night by night. Eventually they'll make a mistake, and then they'll hear your howl, and know they're doomed.<br /> <br /> <b>Elodoth</b><br /> Who knows how you'll catch them in your web? Maybe you'll pull some strings and the tank will be called in for maintenance, letting you pick the crew off at your leisure. Could be that some insurgents/rebels/terrorists will attack the tank and take it out for you. Maybe you'll just watch the crew when they're off-duty, learning their weaknesses then bringing each to a fitting end involving their worst vices and flaws. Maybe one of them will meet a cute boy/girl who persuades them to show them that awesome tank then, suddenly, when they turn roundit's <i>you</i>. Maybe you ward the vehicle park around their tank so that, when you attack, they just can't find their way through the maze of vehicles to the armoured safety of the thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Ithaeur</b><br /> The tank is now possessed by a spirit-ally of yours. Alternatively, it drives into a big hole that your Elemental Influences gouge up in front of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Irraka</b><br /> When one crewman gets out of the tank to have a piss, he never comes back. When they bed down in the apparent safety of the army encampment, you drag one away into the darkness. When they finally seal themselves into it in a fit of absolute terror, you somehow - <i>somehow</i> - are in there already, waiting for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talon</b><br /> You're a soldier, the tank is an objective. It's tougher than an Uratha, can be quite fast, and hits hard, but there are lots of tools designed for taking one out - landmines, AT explosives, etc - and if push comes to shove you, like the Rahu, may be strong enough to rip chunks off the thing. You just need to be careful about getting to it. Also, come in a group with other Blood Talons; one might not be able to tank-tip, but several of you can surely do it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadow</b><br /> A spirit uses its Influences and drinks away the tank's petrol, leaving it stranded and easy prey. Then you call up a blazing pyre underneath it. The prey get out or they cook. If they cook, you rip their ghosts apart just to make sure.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter in Darkness</b><br /> If they go near wilderness, you trap them amidst a knotted tangle of roads and paths that never let them out of that wood again; when they get tired and get out of the tank, you pounce. If you're nowhere near a wood, maybe you just call up a massive eruption of vines and trees underneath and around the tank. Of course, if you've mastered the Gift of Warding then you can just sink your claws into the symbolic nature of the locked access ports on the tank and flick them open with a little bit of will, leaving the prey inside suddenly vulnerable to fang and talon.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Master</b><br /> They're <i>humans</i>. In a <i>tank</i>. They're dead meat. You have two Gifts that are filled with ways to fuck a tank up, this really is no contest. There's a reason humans are your favoured prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords</b><br /> Maybe a sudden storm fills the river and rips the bridge out from under the tank as it crosses. Maybe a dense fog covers the area and you easily sneak up to it under cover, or the weather turns freezing or baking and eventually forces the prey out of their little metal shell. Hilariously, if you manage to get embroiled in a battle with several tanks, you may be able to get another one to shoot the tank that's your actual prey. If you can get to the crew outside of a combat situation, of course, you can probably get them to hand the tank over anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting exposition...<br /> However... all of the things you describe above could be done in 1st Edition, with no need to make any changes whatsoever (and the narratives you provided above even work as described). SO... WHY did the team feel the need to make the changes they made to buff up the Werewolf to the new levels we are seeing? It is the incessant need to BUFF UP werewolves (and even Vampires) that has left such a bad taste in my mouth for the new Editions. Yes, there are some really interesting things there, but in my opinion (which matters little in the grand scheme of things) you did not need to increase their powers to be the unholy terrors that they are now shaping up to be.<br /> <br /> That said, <i><b>Chris</b></i>, I think the work you are doing is awesome (especially some of the fluff changes), though ultimately unneeded in my opinion, at least for me and the group I play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 11-06-2014, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:11:22-08:00","id":304585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304558#post304558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is part of it, perhaps, but the reality is that I think that Gifts and Forms needed no boost at all (though <i><b>maybe </b></i>PU needed something, though I am not even sure about that, to be honest)... and that informs most of my dislike for how 2nd Edition is developing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) First of all - Gifts and Forms needed. Belive me.<br /> 2) As I get it, you dislike, that some werewolves can destroy tank and that's why they no need to hunt (using skills and mind) cuz they can just kill and destroy. But their enemies aren't tanks. Even without crossover (though we know how strong vampires and demons are, and we can image how strong other things will be) there is high-level spirits and stats of azlu, beshilu and other bastards will be changed.<br /> 30 Not any werewolf will have Strenght Gifts. Not even most of them I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:34:30-08:00","id":304626,"title":"","content":"1. They really didn't. Forms and GIfts work quite well for their intended purposes (though some initial gifts could use some clarification, which was provided). Primal Urge could maybe have used a bit more attention, but that is also debatable. But this is one argument that no one wins, since it is so variable of an opinion. Suffice to say I think that the direction that Forms and Gifts took is not my optimal solution. There are some interesting things there, to be sure, but the ramp up in power is not one of them, in my opinion.<br /> 2. You are right, so why design so that you can destroy a tank? Yes, there are tough antagonists, but if they are &quot;High Level Spirits&quot; or other such antagonists, maybe you should think about approaching it in other than a combat mode. Crafting the New Werewolf so that he can power through them is not the solution I would have sought after. We have come back full circle to many of the conceits of cWOD. More power for power's sake. My vampire sucks so buff him up to be a terror right out of the box. My werewolf can't stand against the elder Vampire, so buff him up so he laughs at the elder as he rips him apart. Now, that said, later games (1st Edition - mage and later) did have some amount of adjustment and power build-up due to time in design and the Developers coming into their own. However, the Increase in power levels is a primary concern I have with the 2nd Edition mechanics. It just isn't needed. Chris gave a great exposition on how a 2nd Edition Werewolf would hunt a Tank. The problem with his analysis is that everything he said equally applies to 1st Edition Werewolves. So... if I can use the same tactics in 1st Edition, why the increase in power in 2nd Edition?<br /> 3. Why? They are not restricted to anyone specific. Our long running game has multiple werewolves who have some level of Strength Gifts. They are useful.<br /> <br /> Not trying to be an ass here, just trying to understand. Is it that players/developers did not like the fact that new Vampires/Werewolves were susceptible to a group of thugs with shotguns? Because that is what it seems like to me... Personally, I call that a feature, not a bug. And again, the thugs can be handled, even as a neonate/cub fairly easily, if you give it some thought and attention. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i><b>Claire </b></i>said something up-thread that is interesting to me...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2E werewolves are all scary as hell in a fight, even if they aren't very specialized. The ones who do specialize are terrifying monsters with few peers in battle. Then you also have their pack to deal with... </div> </div> </div>It is interesting, because I hold the same opinion of 1st Edition Werewolves. Based upon a lot of years of playing the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 11-06-2014, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:10:41-08:00","id":304661,"title":"","content":"1. To be honest, I'm not agree with every decision of Developers too. For example, uber-regen - I'd prefer the houserule forms which were published on the forum, they more accurate for characters' progression. But I'm not developer. Anyway, the Gauru-form needed boost cuz average werewolf can use it only 3-5 turn per scene. And gifts didn't became OP because there is almost no 4- or 5-level gifts in 2e. While 4- and 5-dot Disciplines still exists. Btw the first druw of some Gifts (which were showed) seems realy weak for me (5-dot Elodoth or Cunning Nature).<br /> 2. And that the point. 1e werewolf (even elder) can't stand against vampire elder of 2-e. Really, did you see new Celerity rules? I think, just one 2e vampire elder can slay all elder-werewolves from Sighns of the Moon... in the same battle.<br /> Quite high-level vampire (atleast fight orienteted) can destroy tank quite easly. And as I understand the new werewolves antagonists will be boosted too and may be they will be strong enough to destroy it too. So anyway you still will need use your brain for the hunt.<br /> 2.1 About &quot;tank-hunting in 1ed&quot;... Em, nope, you can't. I mean if you use elder with very high PU, may be you can try, but I still can't image what will 1e Elodoth or Irraka will do against the tank.<br /> 3. Probably, cuz not all werewolves are warriors? Some of them can be focused on the social work, spirit magic or stealth missions.<br /> P.S. Question for developers - what about Speed? Will werewolves have something to became faster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:17:05-08:00","id":304667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304626#post304626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. They really didn't. Forms and GIfts work quite well for their intended purposes (though some initial gifts could use some clarification, which was provided). Primal Urge could maybe have used a bit more attention, but that is also debatable. But this is one argument that no one wins, since it is so variable of an opinion. Suffice to say I think that the direction that Forms and Gifts took is not my optimal solution. There are some interesting things there, to be sure, but the ramp up in power is not one of them, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're focusing a bit much on the &quot;power level&quot; side of this.<br /> <br /> It feels to me that the primary motivating factor with how Gifts were changed is not about power level (though PU is getting buffed because it is fairly weak in 1e; I'm not sure what you think is debatable about this). It's about how Gifts and Renown interact. In 1e, Gifts were gated behind expensive Renown costs, had XP penalties for buying ones you wanted out of order, Gift lists often used a wide range or Renown categories in dice pools creating further XP taxes, and so on.<br /> <br /> The new Gift scheme is designed to counteract this. There is a greater positive synergy between Renown and Gifts, since you can focus on one Renown category, and the Facets associated with it, and not get penalized for not buying powers that rely on other Renown traits. The power level of Gifts is also more decoupled from an arbitrary decision about what level that power should be, and more dependent on the investment into the Renown in question. This means Gifts grow more with your character as you invest in Renown and watch their linked facets grow in power.<br /> <br /> The Gift system didn't actually work as well as possible for its intended purpose, which is why its changing. The problem seems to be a bit of conflating how you like things working in your games with the actual intended purpose. But you don't have to switch to 2e. The 1e WtF books have plenty of fun stuff in them to keep a group going for years if you like them more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:50:23-08:00","id":304688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304626#post304626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not trying to be an ass here, just trying to understand. Is it that players/developers did not like the fact that new Vampires/Werewolves were susceptible to a group of thugs with shotguns? Because that is what it seems like to me... Personally, I call that a feature, not a bug. And again, the thugs can be handled, even as a neonate/cub fairly easily, if you give it some thought and attention. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It is interesting, because I hold the same opinion of 1st Edition Werewolves. Based upon a lot of years of playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a contradiction here. You say you think Vamps and Wolves should be susceptible to thugs with shotguns, but you hold the opinion that Vamps and Wolves are scary as hell in a fight.<br /> <br /> Um... If they are susceptible to such mundane methods of defeat, then that doesn't make them scary at all. Part of being scary is that the one being scared should feel powerless. If the shotgun empowers the thug, then he's not afraid of you. He knows he has a chance. That is where the contradiction lies. You can't be &quot;scary as hell in a fight&quot; if the thug feels empowered enough to drop you.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the idea of Vampires and Werewolves being killed by mundane means has never sat well with me. Most of these guys in media show amazing durability vs. mundane means. I'm happy that 2e is reinforcing that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:07:55-08:00","id":304694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304580#post304580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting exposition...<br /> However... all of the things you describe above could be done in 1st Edition, with no need to make any changes whatsoever (and the narratives you provided above even work as described). SO... WHY did the team feel the need to make the changes they made to buff up the Werewolf to the new levels we are seeing? It is the incessant need to BUFF UP werewolves (and even Vampires) that has left such a bad taste in my mouth for the new Editions. Yes, there are some really interesting things there, but in my opinion (which matters little in the grand scheme of things) you did not need to increase their powers to be the unholy terrors that they are now shaping up to be.<br /> <br /> That said, <i><b>Chris</b></i>, I think the work you are doing is awesome (especially some of the fluff changes), though ultimately unneeded in my opinion, at least for me and the group I play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>First? Familiarize yourself with &quot;power creep&quot;; secondly, the design philosophy for splats in the new edition can be summed out as &quot;Monsters out the gate&quot;, ergo, if everyone is getting a power up, the forsaken playerbase would be understandably upset if no bone was thrown their way.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the rules streamlining, nevermind the fluff update, nevermind displaying the actual experience gathered over 10 years.<br /> <br /> Also? Nevermind you can still play any edition as you want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:30:38-08:00","id":304724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304580#post304580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting exposition...<br /> However... all of the things you describe above could be done in 1st Edition, with no need to make any changes whatsoever (and the narratives you provided above even work as described). SO... WHY did the team feel the need to make the changes they made to buff up the Werewolf to the new levels we are seeing? It is the incessant need to BUFF UP werewolves (and even Vampires) that has left such a bad taste in my mouth for the new Editions. Yes, there are some really interesting things there, but in my opinion (which matters little in the grand scheme of things) you did not need to increase their powers to be the unholy terrors that they are now shaping up to be.<br /> <br /> That said, <i><b>Chris</b></i>, I think the work you are doing is awesome (especially some of the fluff changes), though ultimately unneeded in my opinion, at least for me and the group I play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have a go at offering up some insight into <i>why</i> the changes that I've made are occurring later on today once I've sorted out dinner <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the meantime, just want to note that I'm glad that you're happy with how 1e did things, and there's nothing wrong with being happy with an existing edition; I loved 1e and ran many a game with its ruleset, wouldn't have ended up on the 2e writer team if I didn't!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:57:24-08:00","id":304734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304667#post304667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're focusing a bit much on the &quot;power level&quot; side of this.<br /> <br /> It feels to me that the primary motivating factor with how Gifts were changed is not about power level (though PU is getting buffed because it is fairly weak in 1e; I'm not sure what you think is debatable about this). It's about how Gifts and Renown interact. In 1e, Gifts were gated behind expensive Renown costs, had XP penalties for buying ones you wanted out of order, Gift lists often used a wide range or Renown categories in dice pools creating further XP taxes, and so on.<br /> <br /> The new Gift scheme is designed to counteract this. There is a greater positive synergy between Renown and Gifts, since you can focus on one Renown category, and the Facets associated with it, and not get penalized for not buying powers that rely on other Renown traits. The power level of Gifts is also more decoupled from an arbitrary decision about what level that power should be, and more dependent on the investment into the Renown in question. This means Gifts grow more with your character as you invest in Renown and watch their linked facets grow in power.<br /> <br /> The Gift system didn't actually work as well as possible for its intended purpose, which is why its changing. The problem seems to be a bit of conflating how you like things working in your games with the actual intended purpose. But you don't have to switch to 2e. The 1e WtF books have plenty of fun stuff in them to keep a group going for years if you like them more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the PU issue is likely anecdotal. I have never had any issues with its usage in the game, so I see no real need to change it. However, as the lines progressed, the power stats became more &quot;powerful&quot; and usable. Does PU need a like treatment? Maybe.<br /> <br /> Gifts being controlled behind Renown was a brilliant mechanic and was one of the things I really liked. It kept characters from porting to the top of the tier willy nilly, and it forced them to branch out if they wanted to be the best they could be. And I applaud this design treatment. I have played too many games where the quest for the ultimate power overrode the story. This was the perfect brake for such antics. And they still scaled based upon Renown level, because Renown is added to the DP when activating. The fact that you needed all categories of Renown is one of the things I really liked about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have never seen a penalty for <i><b>not </b></i>buying Gifts in 1st Edition, except not having them, which does not change in 2nd Edition. Like I said... Some of the things in the Gifts and Renown section. are pretty interesting. <br /> <br /> As for whether they (gifts in 1st Edition) work as well as they should... that is variable based upon what you are expecting. For Me, they worked EXACTLY like I expected them to, and so I was/am very happy with how they played out (and I was/am very happy with their power levels as well). Others not so much. Over time, other options came forward for some ways to tweak the system to exactly how you wanted it. And these also worked. I do understand that it is more a personal thing than a community thing, in that regard. As for switching editions, I do not plan to do so. However, the few things I DO like in 2nd Edition will likely be ported backwards instead. That is the beauty of the toolbox system. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:03:44-08:00","id":304738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304661#post304661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. To be honest, I'm not agree with every decision of Developers too. For example, uber-regen - I'd prefer the houserule forms which were published on the forum, they more accurate for characters' progression. But I'm not developer. Anyway, the Gauru-form needed boost cuz average werewolf can use it only 3-5 turn per scene. And gifts didn't became OP because there is almost no 4- or 5-level gifts in 2e. While 4- and 5-dot Disciplines still exists. Btw the first druw of some Gifts (which were showed) seems realy weak for me (5-dot Elodoth or Cunning Nature).<br /> 2. And that the point. 1e werewolf (even elder) can't stand against vampire elder of 2-e. Really, did you see new Celerity rules? I think, just one 2e vampire elder can slay all elder-werewolves from Sighns of the Moon... in the same battle.<br /> Quite high-level vampire (atleast fight orienteted) can destroy tank quite easly. And as I understand the new werewolves antagonists will be boosted too and may be they will be strong enough to destroy it too. So anyway you still will need use your brain for the hunt.<br /> 2.1 About &quot;tank-hunting in 1ed&quot;... Em, nope, you can't. I mean if you use elder with very high PU, may be you can try, but I still can't image what will 1e Elodoth or Irraka will do against the tank.<br /> 3. Probably, cuz not all werewolves are warriors? Some of them can be focused on the social work, spirit magic or stealth missions.<br /> P.S. Question for developers - what about Speed? Will werewolves have something to became faster?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry <i><b>TheBadWolf </b></i>- Missed your post...<br /> <br /> 1. Yeah... Regeneration is an odd one now. There are options in 1st Edition to get you where you want to be, and I prefer those to what was spoiled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. Which is a shame, but that is because they boosted Vampires WAY TOO MUCH in my opinion. They did not need it. As for using your brains for the hunt... I would definitely agree... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for Tank Hunting in 1st Edition... Yes you can, My Hunter in Darkness Cahalith did it multiple times. You just have to use your brains and not your brawn. To point... I used non-combat means for the most part, similar in nature to what Chris described earlier up-thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3. Indeed they can. But it is not hard to pick up a little bit of the Strength Gifts. After all, they can be QUITE useful. We have no Rahu in our Group (Cahalith, Itheaur, two Irraka), and yet we all have some level of Strength gifts.<br /> <br /> Father Wolf's Speed covered that in 1st Edition... I would expect that to carry over a bit, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:10:05-08:00","id":304862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304734#post304734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the PU issue is likely anecdotal. I have never had any issues with its usage in the game, so I see no real need to change it. However, as the lines progressed, the power stats became more &quot;powerful&quot; and usable. Does PU need a like treatment? Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a problem with taking the stance of, &quot;I never had a problem so there isn't one.&quot; It is possible to have never run into a problem with a mechanic in your games, and still accept that the mechanic is problematic for other play experiences.<br /> <br /> The question then, is the change actually going to negatively impact your own gaming. Consider how it comes off to say, &quot;I never had a problem with this, and it doesn't matter how many people might have had problems with it, it shouldn't change even if the changes don't actually have a negative effect on how the game will work for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Primal Urge's changes do not sound like they'll actually significantly harm your play style. The 1e version negatively affected lots of people's game experiences. So where's the argument for not changing it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gifts being controlled behind Renown was a brilliant mechanic and was one of the things I really liked. It kept characters from porting to the top of the tier willy nilly, and it forced them to branch out if they wanted to be the best they could be. And I applaud this design treatment. I have played too many games where the quest for the ultimate power overrode the story. This was the perfect brake for such antics. And they still scaled based upon Renown level, because Renown is added to the DP when activating. The fact that you needed all categories of Renown is one of the things I really liked about it. </div> </div> </div>I cannot strongly disagree enough for some key points.<br /> <br /> Designing systems to stop people from playing the games they want is pointless if not down right insulting. You don't want a race to the top game? Don't run a race to the top game with people that don't want to do that. If people enjoy racing to the top the game should let them. The game is about having fun first and foremost, not trying to enshrine a specific approach in the rules. Ultimately, rules can't change play-style preferences. They can only make the game less fun for people interested in engaging in it in a valuable way. Letting people go for high levels of supernatural power if that's what they want to do, does not stop you from playing in games with a different focus. If anything, removing these sorts of barriers actually decreases the incompatibility of these styles because those interested in getting the nifty powers aren't going to be constantly pushing the group to do things that will let them jump through the hoops to get those powers. They can play their way without needing to steal as much spot-light time from everyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have never seen a penalty for <i><b>not </b></i>buying Gifts in 1st Edition, except not having them, which does not change in 2nd Edition. </div> </div> </div>If I have Dominance 1 and I want Dominance 3, but I don't want Dominance 2, my options are to but Dominance 2 anyway, or pay extra XP for Dominance 3.<br /> <br /> This is a penalty for not buying Gifts. It is explicitly so. The new rules eliminate this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for whether they (gifts in 1st Edition) work as well as they should... that is variable based upon what you are expecting. </div> </div> </div>Again, the fact that they work well for you does not mean they worked as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:38:06-08:00","id":304909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304580#post304580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting exposition...<br /> However... all of the things you describe above could be done in 1st Edition, with no need to make any changes whatsoever (and the narratives you provided above even work as described). SO... WHY did the team feel the need to make the changes they made to buff up the Werewolf to the new levels we are seeing? It is the incessant need to BUFF UP werewolves (and even Vampires) that has left such a bad taste in my mouth for the new Editions. Yes, there are some really interesting things there, but in my opinion (which matters little in the grand scheme of things) you did not need to increase their powers to be the unholy terrors that they are now shaping up to be.<br /> <br /> That said, <i><b>Chris</b></i>, I think the work you are doing is awesome (especially some of the fluff changes), though ultimately unneeded in my opinion, at least for me and the group I play with.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, why have we made the changes we have? I can't offer a really in-depth look at this time, but I can give an overview.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I think it's worth noting that any declarations of Uratha being 'buffed' need to be looked at within this <i>specific</i> context: The entirety of Forsaken 2e has not yet been revealed, and it takes place mechanically within the framework of the GMC rules update.<br /> <br /> In terms of the former, for example, not every bit of capacity of the 1e Uratha has made it over to 2e \u2013 no Gifts that allow you to inflict Aggravated damage, for example \u2013 and in terms of the latter it means the core, underlying rules mechanics <i>have already changed</i>. The new Forsaken can't just put up the old Gifts, because even before we get to all the changes we wanted to make with 2e, there are meaningful modifications already in place to eg. the combat system.<br /> <br /> With that pre-existing context out of the way, then, there <i>were</i> a lot of changes we wanted to make in 2e. Gifts aren't just a free-floating part of the system but tie in with all sorts of other aspects. Again, this feeds into a situation where by the time I even get to writing the new Gifts rules, significant alterations to what exists already are definitely on the plate.<br /> <br /> Obviously we had specific goals in mind for the new Werewolf powers, much of which built of our and the community's experience with running Forsaken over the years since its inception. There were all sorts of issues I wanted to address \u2013 the problems with speedbump powers, powers that were unthematic, those with near-broken rules and those with near-useless rules. Given the changes to the underlying structure of how Gifts work (no more linear ascending dots, etc) that we implemented as part of the overhaul of how we wanted the werewolf supernatural powers and Renown to work, I was faced with a situation where large amounts of the existing Gift lists were simply impossible to port anyway, before even looking at those Gifts that were just plain uninspiring or mechanically or thematically 'misses'.<br /> <br /> My guiding goals while writing the new Gifts involved every Facet having an <i>impact</i>, Facets having a meaningful link to the Renown that they represent and/or to the role of the werewolf as a hunter, and no speedbump or spacefiller powers. Would I say that the new Gifts have been 'buffed'? Yes, inasmuch as that they are designed to all be useful and meaningful \u2013 the new werewolves lack several of the powerful old 1e capabilities (no turning yourself into a shadow, shouting healing at packmates or hitting people with lightning bolts) but they also lost a lot of the 'packing material' around the choice Gifts \u2013 you don't have to slog through various dots of a Gift to get the one or two powers in it you actually want.<br /> <br /> The 2e Gifts are less of a total grab-bag of powers and more strongly themed where possible; they have a specific purpose, which is to better equip the Uratha to be the hunter and packmate he or she needs to be. Quite apart from the mechanical issues with 1e Gifts (of which I believe there were many), most of them were a mix of odd tricks taught by spirits, while what a Gift <i>is</i> is now more firmly defined and tied to the Uratha experience.<br /> <br /> It's also my understanding (I may be incorrect) that 1e's Gifts owe a lot in terms of their design and themes to Apocalypse's Gifts. With 2e, there's been less reason to stick to any hold-overs from Apocalypse and more of a push to make Forsaken stand proud in its own right; as someone who never played Apocalypse, I've been happy to work on the new Gifts from the ground up without any particular preconceptions or preferences based off the cWoD gameline, and this may feed into some of the changes as well.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, I feel confident that the new Gift system will be more fun and more engaging than the old one for most groups, that the Facets will feel more impactful and more appropriate for Uratha, and that the whole package will help make Renown a more enjoyable element to engage with as well. I'm not particularly fussed about overall or comparative 'power level', buffing or nerfing \u2013 rather, I want a given power to feel meaningful and have a definite impact on the game mechanically and thematically. Where Gifts stood, power-wise, in 1e is not important to me when designing them in the framework of 2e, which is the context in which they will actually have to perform.<br /> <br /> The new Gifts system may not work for every group. That's fine \u2013 great, even, if you're happy with the old system, since it means you already have something that works for you, and that's the aim of game design! However, for many people the old Gifts system was <i>not</i> working for them, and in 2e I have endeavoured to create something new that will.<br /> <br /> I hope that, once 2e is released, everyone will have an edition of Werewolf that they can enjoy, whether that's sticking with 1e, moving to 2e or nabbing bits of each edition for a hybrid to their preference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:46:01-08:00","id":304915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304909#post304909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, why have we made the changes we have? I can't offer a really in-depth look at this time, but I can give an overview.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I think it's worth noting that any declarations of Uratha being 'buffed' need to be looked at within this <i>specific</i> context: The entirety of Forsaken 2e has not yet been revealed, and it takes place mechanically within the framework of the GMC rules update.<br /> <br /> In terms of the former, for example, not every bit of capacity of the 1e Uratha has made it over to 2e \u2013 no Gifts that allow you to inflict Aggravated damage, for example \u2013 and in terms of the latter it means the core, underlying rules mechanics <i>have already changed</i>. The new Forsaken can't just put up the old Gifts, because even before we get to all the changes we wanted to make with 2e, there are meaningful modifications already in place to eg. the combat system.<br /> <br /> With that pre-existing context out of the way, then, there <i>were</i> a lot of changes we wanted to make in 2e. Gifts aren't just a free-floating part of the system but tie in with all sorts of other aspects. Again, this feeds into a situation where by the time I even get to writing the new Gifts rules, significant alterations to what exists already are definitely on the plate.<br /> <br /> Obviously we had specific goals in mind for the new Werewolf powers, much of which built of our and the community's experience with running Forsaken over the years since its inception. There were all sorts of issues I wanted to address \u2013 the problems with speedbump powers, powers that were unthematic, those with near-broken rules and those with near-useless rules. Given the changes to the underlying structure of how Gifts work (no more linear ascending dots, etc) that we implemented as part of the overhaul of how we wanted the werewolf supernatural powers and Renown to work, I was faced with a situation where large amounts of the existing Gift lists were simply impossible to port anyway, before even looking at those Gifts that were just plain uninspiring or mechanically or thematically 'misses'.<br /> <br /> My guiding goals while writing the new Gifts involved every Facet having an <i>impact</i>, Facets having a meaningful link to the Renown that they represent and/or to the role of the werewolf as a hunter, and no speedbump or spacefiller powers. Would I say that the new Gifts have been 'buffed'? Yes, inasmuch as that they are designed to all be useful and meaningful \u2013 the new werewolves lack several of the powerful old 1e capabilities (no turning yourself into a shadow, shouting healing at packmates or hitting people with lightning bolts) but they also lost a lot of the