u already have something that works for you, and that's the aim of game design! However, for many people the old Gifts system was <i>not</i> working for them, and in 2e I have endeavoured to create something new that will.<br /> <br /> I hope that, once 2e is released, everyone will have an edition of Werewolf that they can enjoy, whether that's sticking with 1e, moving to 2e or nabbing bits of each edition for a hybrid to their preference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While Werewolf is not my favourite foray into the NWoD, but as someone who does plan on getting the 2nd edition at some point I really appreciate posts like this. As I consider myself someone who has some apprehensions about the 2nd editions so far as far as power levels go. Really helps set up a benefit of the doubt for enjoying the materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:14:14-08:00","id":304938,"title":"","content":"The 2E Gifts are really a thing of beauty. One of the biggest complaints with <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b>was the dreaded &quot;What do we <i>do</i>?&quot; Or some variant involving spirit cops. It was charged with not really jumping out at you, nothing sinking its fangs into your throat. While I loved even first edition, second is much, much stronger. It's better designed mechanically, as is the way of the 2E games. It's <i>much </i>better designed thematically, as everything has been rebuilt to really give a strong focus on theme and meaning. When you read it, you'll no longer wonder just what you do with it. You'll write up a pack, get that blood pumping and those paws thumping. You'll have drama as you and your closest family follow your calling. You have lots of reason to interact with humans as well as the strange spirits across the Gauntlet. As a werewolf, both in-character and out of character, you'll get to experience a lot of different perspectives in a single character. Everything reinforces this theme, too, from Gifts to werewolf template conditions to the hunt itself.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to get the reactions from folks once 2E drops.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:31:01-08:00","id":304949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304862#post304862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a problem with taking the stance of, &quot;I never had a problem so there isn't one.&quot; It is possible to have never run into a problem with a mechanic in your games, and still accept that the mechanic is problematic for other play experiences.<br /> <br /> The question then, is the change actually going to negatively impact your own gaming. Consider how it comes off to say, &quot;I never had a problem with this, and it doesn't matter how many people might have had problems with it, it shouldn't change even if the changes don't actually have a negative effect on how the game will work for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Primal Urge's changes do not sound like they'll actually significantly harm your play style. The 1e version negatively affected lots of people's game experiences. So where's the argument for not changing it?<br /> <br /> <br /> I cannot strongly disagree enough for some key points.<br /> <br /> Designing systems to stop people from playing the games they want is pointless if not down right insulting. You don't want a race to the top game? Don't run a race to the top game with people that don't want to do that. If people enjoy racing to the top the game should let them. The game is about having fun first and foremost, not trying to enshrine a specific approach in the rules. Ultimately, rules can't change play-style preferences. They can only make the game less fun for people interested in engaging in it in a valuable way. Letting people go for high levels of supernatural power if that's what they want to do, does not stop you from playing in games with a different focus. If anything, removing these sorts of barriers actually decreases the incompatibility of these styles because those interested in getting the nifty powers aren't going to be constantly pushing the group to do things that will let them jump through the hoops to get those powers. They can play their way without needing to steal as much spot-light time from everyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I have Dominance 1 and I want Dominance 3, but I don't want Dominance 2, my options are to but Dominance 2 anyway, or pay extra XP for Dominance 3.<br /> <br /> This is a penalty for not buying Gifts. It is explicitly so. The new rules eliminate this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, the fact that they work well for you does not mean they worked as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see and understand some of the points you bring up, to be sure.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Penalty&quot; for skipping Gifts in the Tree... I don't see it as such. I pay a Pittance of XP to gain something without having to go through something I do not want. In your example... If I don't want to pay for Dominance 2, I do not see the 3 XP cost as a penalty. It is a benefit to me that I get to skip something without purchasing it. It is a boon (because I get to skip purchasing something I do not want), not a penalty. The penalty would be to tell me to suck it up and just purchase Dominance 2, even though I do not want it. Fundamental Differences in Viewpoint, I guess...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:37:57-08:00","id":304956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304909#post304909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, why have we made the changes we have? I can't offer a really in-depth look at this time, but I can give an overview.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I think it's worth noting that any declarations of Uratha being 'buffed' need to be looked at within this <i>specific</i> context: The entirety of Forsaken 2e has not yet been revealed, and it takes place mechanically within the framework of the GMC rules update.<br /> <br /> In terms of the former, for example, not every bit of capacity of the 1e Uratha has made it over to 2e \u2013 no Gifts that allow you to inflict Aggravated damage, for example \u2013 and in terms of the latter it means the core, underlying rules mechanics <i>have already changed</i>. The new Forsaken can't just put up the old Gifts, because even before we get to all the changes we wanted to make with 2e, there are meaningful modifications already in place to eg. the combat system.<br /> <br /> With that pre-existing context out of the way, then, there <i>were</i> a lot of changes we wanted to make in 2e. Gifts aren't just a free-floating part of the system but tie in with all sorts of other aspects. Again, this feeds into a situation where by the time I even get to writing the new Gifts rules, significant alterations to what exists already are definitely on the plate.<br /> <br /> Obviously we had specific goals in mind for the new Werewolf powers, much of which built of our and the community's experience with running Forsaken over the years since its inception. There were all sorts of issues I wanted to address \u2013 the problems with speedbump powers, powers that were unthematic, those with near-broken rules and those with near-useless rules. Given the changes to the underlying structure of how Gifts work (no more linear ascending dots, etc) that we implemented as part of the overhaul of how we wanted the werewolf supernatural powers and Renown to work, I was faced with a situation where large amounts of the existing Gift lists were simply impossible to port anyway, before even looking at those Gifts that were just plain uninspiring or mechanically or thematically 'misses'.<br /> <br /> My guiding goals while writing the new Gifts involved every Facet having an <i>impact</i>, Facets having a meaningful link to the Renown that they represent and/or to the role of the werewolf as a hunter, and no speedbump or spacefiller powers. Would I say that the new Gifts have been 'buffed'? Yes, inasmuch as that they are designed to all be useful and meaningful \u2013 the new werewolves lack several of the powerful old 1e capabilities (no turning yourself into a shadow, shouting healing at packmates or hitting people with lightning bolts) but they also lost a lot of the 'packing material' around the choice Gifts \u2013 you don't have to slog through various dots of a Gift to get the one or two powers in it you actually want.<br /> <br /> The 2e Gifts are less of a total grab-bag of powers and more strongly themed where possible; they have a specific purpose, which is to better equip the Uratha to be the hunter and packmate he or she needs to be. Quite apart from the mechanical issues with 1e Gifts (of which I believe there were many), most of them were a mix of odd tricks taught by spirits, while what a Gift <i>is</i> is now more firmly defined and tied to the Uratha experience.<br /> <br /> It's also my understanding (I may be incorrect) that 1e's Gifts owe a lot in terms of their design and themes to Apocalypse's Gifts. With 2e, there's been less reason to stick to any hold-overs from Apocalypse and more of a push to make Forsaken stand proud in its own right; as someone who never played Apocalypse, I've been happy to work on the new Gifts from the ground up without any particular preconceptions or preferences based off the cWoD gameline, and this may feed into some of the changes as well.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, I feel confident that the new Gift system will be more fun and more engaging than the old one for most groups, that the Facets will feel more impactful and more appropriate for Uratha, and that the whole package will help make Renown a more enjoyable element to engage with as well. I'm not particularly fussed about overall or comparative 'power level', buffing or nerfing \u2013 rather, I want a given power to feel meaningful and have a definite impact on the game mechanically and thematically. Where Gifts stood, power-wise, in 1e is not important to me when designing them in the framework of 2e, which is the context in which they will actually have to perform.<br /> <br /> The new Gifts system may not work for every group. That's fine \u2013 great, even, if you're happy with the old system, since it means you already have something that works for you, and that's the aim of game design! However, for many people the old Gifts system was <i>not</i> working for them, and in 2e I have endeavoured to create something new that will.<br /> <br /> I hope that, once 2e is released, everyone will have an edition of Werewolf that they can enjoy, whether that's sticking with 1e, moving to 2e or nabbing bits of each edition for a hybrid to their preference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome... Thanks for the Insight <i><b>Chris</b></i>...<br /> As I have said numerous times... you guys are performing a hell of a job. Wish I could get past the Design Elements of GMC so that I could enjoy them in their native format. Many of the things I like in 2nd Edition are destined to show up in our games as conversion to 1st. Have a great day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:41:21-08:00","id":304960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304938#post304938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2E Gifts are really a thing of beauty. One of the biggest complaints with <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b>was the dreaded &quot;What do we <i>do</i>?&quot; Or some variant involving spirit cops. It was charged with not really jumping out at you, nothing sinking its fangs into your throat. While I loved even first edition, second is much, much stronger. It's better designed mechanically, as is the way of the 2E games. It's <i>much </i>better designed thematically, as everything has been rebuilt to really give a strong focus on theme and meaning. When you read it, you'll no longer wonder just what you do with it. You'll write up a pack, get that blood pumping and those paws thumping. You'll have drama as you and your closest family follow your calling. You have lots of reason to interact with humans as well as the strange spirits across the Gauntlet. As a werewolf, both in-character and out of character, you'll get to experience a lot of different perspectives in a single character. Everything reinforces this theme, too, from Gifts to werewolf template conditions to the hunt itself.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to get the reactions from folks once 2E drops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting observation, since I always considered Werewolf to be fairly intuitive with the &quot;What do we do&quot; question. And have enjoyed the drama unfolding (that you describe at the end of your post) from the very beginning of Forsaken. Maybe I am just odd... Maybe our whole group is just Odd... would not be the first time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for taking the time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:40:28-08:00","id":305020,"title":"","content":"I don't mean that it was impossible to figure out what to do, or that themes were nonexistent. I loved <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> 1st edition as much as anyone. But what I mean is that we really shaped the new edition into something that reinforces those themes and gives even more options. No one will have trouble reading 2E and figuring out &quot;What do we do?&quot; And they won't find Gifts boring or underpowered, nor will they feel the game boils down to essentially &quot;spirit cops.&quot; They'll realize it's rich and dramatic, evoking powerful, primal feelings amid an urban jungle setting.<br /> <br /> See, we didn't have to <i>add </i>those things. We just reinforced them, brought them welling to the surface like blood pooling in a wound. We tore open the skin to let you gnaw at the bones holding this beast together. More than ever, 2E has its own identity and some really strong core themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:47:48-08:00","id":305027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305020#post305020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean that it was impossible to figure out what to do, or that themes were nonexistent. I loved <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> 1st edition as much as anyone. But what I mean is that we really shaped the new edition into something that reinforces those themes and gives even more options. No one will have trouble reading 2E and figuring out &quot;What do we do?&quot; And they won't find Gifts boring or underpowered, nor will they feel the game boils down to essentially &quot;spirit cops.&quot; They'll realize it's rich and dramatic, evoking powerful, primal feelings amid an urban jungle setting.<br /> <br /> See, we didn't have to <i>add </i>those things. We just reinforced them, brought them welling to the surface like blood pooling in a wound. We tore open the skin to let you gnaw at the bones holding this beast together. More than ever, 2E has its own identity and some really strong core themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes Sense... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Like I said... I wish it wasn't tied to the GMC rules set. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:50:00-08:00","id":305029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=304949#post304949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see and understand some of the points you bring up, to be sure.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Penalty&quot; for skipping Gifts in the Tree... I don't see it as such. I pay a Pittance of XP to gain something without having to go through something I do not want. In your example... If I don't want to pay for Dominance 2, I do not see the 3 XP cost as a penalty. It is a benefit to me that I get to skip something without purchasing it. It is a boon (because I get to skip purchasing something I do not want), not a penalty. The penalty would be to tell me to suck it up and just purchase Dominance 2, even though I do not want it. Fundamental Differences in Viewpoint, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the argument both ways on this. For one, I can argue that I save the experience I would have used to purchase a gift I didn't want at the cost of spending a measly 3 additional experience to purchase the one I do want. On the other side, players like me are thinking about why are we required to pay an additional tax of experience at all? If they are going to allow you to purchase dots without a prerequisite, why bother making them tiered in the first place? The new system proposed is very appealing to me since now it allows me to select the gifts I want for what is thematic, rather than realizing I need to waste 12 experience just to grab that 1 gift at the end of a tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the PU issue is likely anecdotal. I have never had any issues with its usage in the game, so I see no real need to change it. However, as the lines progressed, the power stats became more &quot;powerful&quot; and usable. Does PU need a like treatment? Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the biggest issue with Primal Urge and other power stats in 1e was that it was extremely costly and of not a great deal of use to raise it beyond 3. Rarely would you see someone take a power stat to 4, and in 8 years of playing Werewolf, I have NEVER seen a player take a power stat to 6+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:07:29-08:00","id":305045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305029#post305029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see the argument both ways on this. For one, I can argue that I save the experience I would have used to purchase a gift I didn't want at the cost of spending a measly 3 additional experience to purchase the one I do want. On the other side, players like me are thinking about why are we required to pay an additional tax of experience at all? If they are going to allow you to purchase dots without a prerequisite, why bother making them tiered in the first place? The new system proposed is very appealing to me since now it allows me to select the gifts I want for what is thematic, rather than realizing I need to waste 12 experience just to grab that 1 gift at the end of a tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is a toss-up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the biggest issue with Primal Urge and other power stats in 1e was that it was extremely costly and of not a great deal of use to raise it beyond 3. Rarely would you see someone take a power stat to 4, and in 8 years of playing Werewolf, I have NEVER seen a player take a power stat to 6+. </div> </div> </div>In all the years we played, we currently have a PC with a PU of 5 and one with a PU4, the others (2) are PU3. We never saw one go above 5, but that is okay. Our current game has gone on for 500+ Experience. I believe that my Character (the Cahalith with a PU4) has the most gifts with 28 of them (ore so), and 20 Renown. Gifts/Renown/PU has worked well for us over the years. They fits our play-styles very well. Which is probably why I have issues with the transition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:15:52-08:00","id":305050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305029#post305029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the biggest issue with Primal Urge and other power stats in 1e was that it was extremely costly and of not a great deal of use to raise it beyond 3. Rarely would you see someone take a power stat to 4, and in 8 years of playing Werewolf, I have NEVER seen a player take a power stat to 6+.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done that, actually. I had a character I played in the Camarilla (now Mind's Eye Society), back when I was a member. Now, mind you, the amount of Experience in that setting is a bit higher if you compare to, say, the suggested totals in the book for more experienced characters. Still, At his most powerful in terms of PU and such, prior to a &quot;Soft Reset&quot; (re-jiggling of XP totals, in this case to lower them to more manageable levels), my character had the following &quot;high-stat&quot; levels:<br /> <br /> -PU 7<br /> -Composure 6<br /> -Harmony 8<br /> -Purity 5<br /> <br /> This was also where I found out quite by happenstance how good of an Attribute Composure is. I got it that high because of the character's nature, without thinking (at the time) of what else it effects on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> Still, as I was AMST Forsaken at the time (translation: Global-level Forsaken Storyteller for the entire club), I kept the character as much in the background as I could. He didn't really get too terribly involved in things, had no leadership or other influential position, nothing. His only claim to &quot;fame,&quot; from an in-character perspective, was that he was very publicly known as a member of the Lodge of Ashes. So, you know, there was that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:07:02-08:00","id":305084,"title":"","content":"The thematic tightening of Disciplines was my favorite part of Vampire 2e. It went from a grab-bag of powers roughly associated with different versions of vampires to a tight set of abilities firmly tied to their predatory nature. When I read it, the first thing I thought was &quot;I really hope they do this with Werewolf&quot;. Suffice to say, I'm thrilled. When Forsaken first came out, my group played two two year long campaigns back-to-back and so we are very familiar with all of the weak points that Chris elucidates. Even without the book, I'm planning my next campaign. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:01:47-08:00","id":305114,"title":"","content":"Alright, so moving away from the current topic I have a question for the devs and/ or writers. Is it possible now to play a lone wolf without suffering for it, or is it still mandatory to be part of a pack?<br /> <br /> In 1e it was highly frowned upon and was even a Harmony sin. Is this still the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 11-06-2014, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:15:39-08:00","id":305117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305114#post305114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so moving away from the current topic I have a question for the devs and/ or writers. Is it possible now to play a lone wolf without suffering for it, or is it still mandatory to be part of a pack?<br /> <br /> In 1e it was highly frowned upon and was even a Harmony sin. Is this still the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some really neat Lone Wolf rules in the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide (don't remember which part though...)<br /> <br /> Will they still be applicable in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:40:29-08:00","id":305203,"title":"","content":"I think being without a pack, or staying away from yours for too long, would clearly be a breaking point for Harmony towards the Man side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T00:40:05-08:00","id":305406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305203#post305203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think being without a pack, or staying away from yours for too long, would clearly be a breaking point for Harmony towards the Man side of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I agree. Having a pack is pretty human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T01:22:04-08:00","id":305439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305406#post305406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I agree. Having a pack is pretty human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are social animals. Werewolves are pack animals \u2014 psychologically geared to require a hunting party, which spills out into a larger group of Wolf-Blooded and humans. The &quot;typical&quot; model for a werewolf pack in 2e is a gang, but that's just the easiest reference point. Think of any tight-knit group that acts as a surrogate family, from soldiers to investment bankers to Freemasons.<br /> <br /> It's a breaking point towards Flesh to run without a pack, but you can get around that by deliberately reinforcing your Uratha nature in other ways to break towards Spirit, thus giving you a chance to maintain the balance. It does make things like the Siskur-Dah harder \u2014 it's a rite, and while you can work it alone you only get your tribe's version. You also don't get the benefit of having a powerful totem. The character can make it work, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T03:32:54-08:00","id":305480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305027#post305027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes Sense... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Like I said... I wish it wasn't tied to the GMC rules set. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You should really try it to run. Myself, I was at first fearful with Conditions, Tits, Beats and new Virtue &amp; Vice system. But I trusted developers - and it repaid. New system ( GMC rules ) <b>looks</b> as complicated, but it's only because of &quot;paradigm shifts&quot; for old players - after couple of weeks with adjustments, I <b>loved</b> it. Really, really do.<br /> <br /> Conditions are &quot;excuses to get penalty or bonuses&quot; that in 1ed WoD were somehow &quot;taken from air&quot;. Now you see this like you are Shocked, your Uratha is in this Form, and he get this and this Tilt in combat - it's more coharant and in reality - tells a stories in to itself. If you will want to try, I could advise you some things to do or look for from my year of running both <b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Mage</b> on GMC rules now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:34:37-08:00","id":305622,"title":"","content":"Btw, what about Inspiration Gifts? They useful for social plaing, or just buff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:51:19-08:00","id":305638,"title":"","content":"We had some explanations of the Gift of Inspiration <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115780-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-gifts-this-time-for-real?p=239092#post239092\">here.</a><br /> <br /> I like the cunning one but the glory one has a nice passive effect, providing it's passive..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T07:08:41-08:00","id":305650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305480#post305480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should really try it to run. Myself, I was at first fearful with Conditions, Tits, Beats and new Virtue &amp; Vice system. But I trusted developers - and it repaid. New system ( GMC rules ) <b>looks</b> as complicated, but it's only because of &quot;paradigm shifts&quot; for old players - after couple of weeks with adjustments, I <b>loved</b> it. Really, really do.<br /> <br /> Conditions are &quot;excuses to get penalty or bonuses&quot; that in 1ed WoD were somehow &quot;taken from air&quot;. Now you see this like you are Shocked, your Uratha is in this Form, and he get this and this Tilt in combat - it's more coharant and in reality - tells a stories in to itself. If you will want to try, I could advise you some things to do or look for from my year of running both <b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Mage</b> on GMC rules now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who says we haven't tried it?<br /> <br /> Problem is that I think that Fate does it better, with less clutter. So, if I want something akin to a 2nd Edition GMC style game, I just use Fate. My World of Darkness Campaign Setting is Fate Based, not GMC, for that very reason. Sorry, but Conditions, Tilts, Beats and the new Virtue /Vice system feel tacked on and forced (coming from 1st Edition), whereas Fate was designed that way from the ground up. It flows far more naturally in Fate then in GMC, at least for us, and the stories just flow so naturally that we sometimes have a difficult time choosing which stories to pursue, there are so many of them... Combine that with other Mechanical bits that I have not cared for (in Blood and Smoke/GMC obviously because otherwise all we have is spoilers) and the decision is very easy for me.<br /> <br /> I will still pull 2nd Edition stuff out and port back to 1st Edition, or translate it to Fate, but I have no actual interest in playing/running 2nd Edition right now. The fluff is amazing, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T07:20:23-08:00","id":305658,"title":"","content":"You realise that FATE wasn't designed that way from the ground up, but is a dramatic editing mechanic slapped onto a older game called FUDGE, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T07:45:11-08:00","id":305673,"title":"","content":"Fate is not Fudge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But yes, I know that (And FATE CORE is a complete redesign from the bottom up). That does not change the fact that I think it runs more smoothly than GMC does. I think that Fate does it Better. Fate feels less clunky (well, not clunky at all, in my opinion). The one place that Fate is lacking is in Fluff (which you guys do better in), since it is incumbent upon the Group to create the Fluff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 11-07-2014, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:07:01-08:00","id":305868,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Starting to look a lot like edition warring here, albeit an unusually civil discourse. Either way, the topic of FATE and Edition preference is certainly thread-capping. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:11:23-08:00","id":305873,"title":"","content":"Moving back to the topic,<br /> <br /> Was Werewolf 2e built around balance to itself, or balance against the entire game as a whole? I know that people love to do those white room tests, but it is pretty much meaningless if they were never designed with that intent in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:56:41-08:00","id":305942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305873#post305873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving back to the topic,<br /> <br /> Was Werewolf 2e built around balance to itself, or balance against the entire game as a whole? I know that people love to do those white room tests, but it is pretty much meaningless if they were never designed with that intent in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my point of view in the parts that I wrote, balance to itself. How can I even balance it against the entire game when the only one that's been written yet is Vampire 2e? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not that I consider an attempt at balance with the other gamelines to necessarily be desirable anyway, and a serious minefield when considering the different strengths and weaknesses of the various supernatural types.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that I simply <i>ignored</i> the existence of the other lines - I specifically worked on Werewolf's mental-influencing and social powers to be different to Vampire's, and lacking in certain arenas (vampires remain better at just twisting your mind into a pretzel and making you do what they want like a puppet). When writing particular powers (like a specific one of the Warding Gift Facets) I took into account the existence of various gameline powers around gates, portals, scrying etc and made sure that the Facet made reference to how it interacts with such. What I <i>didn't</i> do is try to build the Werewolf supernatural powers to make them equal to Vampires or Mages, or to follow some other pre-defined hierarchy of power with other lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:29:00-08:00","id":305997,"title":"","content":"Thematically, are moon gifts the only ones meant to go 1-5, while all other gifts are faceted? Or would there be support for Shadow or Wolf gifts that go from 1-5?<br /> <br /> Also, are there conceivably more moon gifts than those belonging to the standard five auspices? Just offhand in 1e we had Tainted Moon and Dreamer, Judge, Stalker, Warrior and Witch moons, as well as the Eclipse gifts, in addition to the auspices. In addition the later 1e books offered 'rare' auspices like Blood Moon and Solar/Lunar/Stellar Eclipse. Obviously (or at least, based on what we've been told so far) extraneous stuff like that won't be in the 2e core but as developers would they be appropriate fits for the game and if so would the 1-5 moon gift be the way to go with them?<br /> <br /> Or should I be asking this on the blog for Mr Wilson's ask and answer entry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-07-2014, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:04:02-08:00","id":306067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=305997#post305997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically, are moon gifts the only ones meant to go 1-5, while all other gifts are faceted? Or would there be support for Shadow or Wolf gifts that go from 1-5?<br /> <br /> Also, are there conceivably more moon gifts than those belonging to the standard five auspices? Just offhand in 1e we had Tainted Moon and Dreamer, Judge, Stalker, Warrior and Witch moons, as well as the Eclipse gifts, in addition to the auspices. In addition the later 1e books offered 'rare' auspices like Blood Moon and Solar/Lunar/Stellar Eclipse. Obviously (or at least, based on what we've been told so far) extraneous stuff like that won't be in the 2e core but as developers would they be appropriate fits for the game and if so would the 1-5 moon gift be the way to go with them?<br /> <br /> Or should I be asking this on the blog for Mr Wilson's ask and answer entry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moon Gifts are the only Gifts that have kept the ascending 1-5 dots ladder.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are more Moon Gifts than the standard 5 - I'd have liked to put two Moon Gifts per Auspice into the core but we just didn't have the space. The Gifts rules include how you go about acquiring additional Moon Gifts to future-proof for the inclusion of new ones in future supplements. Yes, such Gifts will use the ascending 1-5 dots ladder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:21:03-08:00","id":306081,"title":"","content":"Thank you, I like the facet set up but I can see times it might be nice to have more of a traditional scaling. It will be interesting to see if gaining renown works the same way in-game as before.<br /> <br /> So in this case, gifts granted from lodges are likely to be faceted, unless they are somehow involved with the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T13:49:30-08:00","id":306091,"title":"","content":"(Pure speculation because lodge design is still under discussion)<br /> <br /> If a lodge grants a unique Gift it will be faceted. The (incredibly rare, I would think) exceptions would be lodges dedicated to a single Auspice, which could possibly grant a new Moon Gift with 1-5 levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T16:10:44-08:00","id":306198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306091#post306091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Pure speculation because lodge design is still under discussion)<br /> <br /> If a lodge grants a unique Gift it will be faceted. The (incredibly rare, I would think) exceptions would be lodges dedicated to a single Auspice, which could possibly grant a new Moon Gift with 1-5 levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have touched upon one of my biggest hopes in regards to lodges. In my ideal world, the lodges would be a bit more defined than they were in 1e in regards to benefits granted. I had no problem with the lore aspect of the lodges and greatly enjoyed many of them. However, many of the lodges felt inferior due to the massive amount of benefits some received for no apparent reason, while others received almost nothing. A good example would be between the Lodge of Voices and the Lodge of Swords","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T19:51:11-08:00","id":306344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306198#post306198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have touched upon one of my biggest hopes in regards to lodges. In my ideal world, the lodges would be a bit more defined than they were in 1e in regards to benefits granted. I had no problem with the lore aspect of the lodges and greatly enjoyed many of them. However, many of the lodges felt inferior due to the massive amount of benefits some received for no apparent reason, while others received almost nothing. A good example would be between the Lodge of Voices and the Lodge of Swords</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I love lodges. We've had some discussion (as I think we've mentioned before), so hopefully we'll get some stuff sorted at some point. Of course, any plan or idea or what-have-you about getting that out to you folks is above my pay grade. Still, with the Werewolf love we've got on the team, I'm sure the final result will be badass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T03:19:08-08:00","id":306508,"title":"","content":"For folks really into Werewolf:The Forsaken. Is there are particular, singular feature change or update to the game you can't wait to try out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T06:26:43-08:00","id":306631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306081#post306081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, I like the facet set up but I can see times it might be nice to have more of a traditional scaling. It will be interesting to see if gaining renown works the same way in-game as before.<br /> <br /> So in this case, gifts granted from lodges are likely to be faceted, unless they are somehow involved with the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much my <i>personal opinion</i> and by no means an official stance or anything, but I am strongly opposed to Gifts that are restricted to specific Lodges; unless a Lodge's Totem is utterly specific and unique in its symbolism, it shouldn't be the only spirit capable of inflicting a given Gift.<br /> <br /> That said, <i>if</i> a Gift were granted by a Lodge, it would indeed be split into the five Renown Facets unless a Moon Gift, in which case it would be split into five ascending Facets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T06:35:49-08:00","id":306633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306344#post306344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I love lodges. We've had some discussion (as I think we've mentioned before), so hopefully we'll get some stuff sorted at some point. Of course, any plan or idea or what-have-you about getting that out to you folks is above my pay grade. Still, with the Werewolf love we've got on the team, I'm sure the final result will be badass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup; am planning to do a specific Lodge draft to put up on the writer list given the discussions we've had about how 2e Lodges should look, but it'll be at least a couple of weeks before I can work on it as am very busy with other stuff atm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T07:19:57-08:00","id":306646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306508#post306508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For folks really into Werewolf:The Forsaken. Is there are particular, singular feature change or update to the game you can't wait to try out?</div> </div> </div> </div>New social gifts. And I want to tests Gauru (official vs houseruled)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T09:18:01-08:00","id":306696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306631#post306631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very much my <i>personal opinion</i> and by no means an official stance or anything, but I am strongly opposed to Gifts that are restricted to specific Lodges; unless a Lodge's Totem is utterly specific and unique in its symbolism, it shouldn't be the only spirit capable of inflicting a given Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on your personal opinion, should that include Moon Gifts, or are the Lunes and Luna more picky? First edition had a lot of gifts, but many were limited to auspice or tribe or lodge, which cut down on the amount an individual werewolf could find. I actually agree with your opinion, but I think for simplicity's sake it wouldn't be unreasonable to have Gift write-ups in Lodge entries, appreciating that, 'Anyone can get this gift from this totem spirit, but this lodge tends to have it more than others due to their closeness to it.' Of course, that depends on how Gifts are obtained by Werewolves, Inflicted suggests gaining gifts isn't solely a blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306508#post306508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For folks really into Werewolf:The Forsaken. Is there are particular, singular feature change or update to the game you can't wait to try out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never really that into the auspices and tribes before, always just picked Ithaeur Bone Shadow, but since their write-up and the teaser I've been itching to see them all and finally am tempted to go with something different. Also the Harmony and Blood and Bone system, we had a lot of fun with the new systems in Blood and Smoke but it will be nice to see one where you can action your way up the scale. The big thing is probably the Siskur-Dah, we'll probably try and have one right out the gate.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller I'm also interested in seeing how the revamped antagonists are set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2014, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:36:08-08:00","id":308345,"title":"","content":"What are the chance to see Forsaken 2ed before Christmas? I plan a YouTube channel with reviews of RPG books, and would like to know were to look for the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T10:51:45-08:00","id":309315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=306696#post306696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on your personal opinion, should that include Moon Gifts, or are the Lunes and Luna more picky? First edition had a lot of gifts, but many were limited to auspice or tribe or lodge, which cut down on the amount an individual werewolf could find. I actually agree with your opinion, but I think for simplicity's sake it wouldn't be unreasonable to have Gift write-ups in Lodge entries, appreciating that, 'Anyone can get this gift from this totem spirit, but this lodge tends to have it more than others due to their closeness to it.' Of course, that depends on how Gifts are obtained by Werewolves, Inflicted suggests gaining gifts isn't solely a blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not yet sure on Moon Gifts; I can see some argument for more restricted access to specific Moon Gifts that specific Lunes are caretakers of. In theory, any Moon Gift is an extension of the quicksilver communion with the Warden Moon itself during the First Change, and require no more outside influence than already exists in Luna's link to the Uratha's spirit, but it could be that Lunes guard particularly esoteric symbols linked to the Auspice that they can mark a werewolf with.<br /> <br /> I think I'd tend more towards such Moon Gifts being accessible by undertaking a spirit quest to track down the specific Lune with the Gift in question, but I can see situations where a given Lune with an agenda might decide that it wants a Lodge of werewolves tasked with a particular purpose to which the Gift is well-suited (or for which it can dangle the Gift as a carrot/reward for service).<br /> <br /> Gifts are always beneficial to the recipient, but receiving them may not be the most pleasant experience - take a look at my story in the fiction Anthology for hints at that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, I could see mileage for 'cursed' Gifts or Gifts that come with significant drawbacks as well as powers, because of what happens in how a Gift is gained. Interesting notion to mull over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=308345#post308345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the chance to see Forsaken 2ed before Christmas? I plan a YouTube channel with reviews of RPG books, and would like to know were to look for the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no inside knowledge on this, but I'd note that the art direction part of the Monday update has some info, so I guess it depends how long it takes artists to get their work in.<br /> <br /> I know that when I used to work for another company and did some art direction there, we had a turnaround of 2 weeks to a month for artists to get work in, but that was working to a particularly frantic timetable and I don't know whether OP run a more relaxed schedule <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T11:07:44-08:00","id":309325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=309315#post309315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts are always beneficial to the recipient, but receiving them may not be the most pleasant experience - take a look at my story in the fiction Anthology for hints at that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, I could see mileage for 'cursed' Gifts or Gifts that come with significant drawbacks as well as powers, because of what happens in how a Gift is gained. Interesting notion to mull over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man I would love a line of cursed gifts that provide great power and great cost. Good for those people who want to play an Uratha with a very fatalistic outlook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:53:39-08:00","id":313312,"title":"","content":"So there will not be a blog post this week? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:39:04-08:00","id":313327,"title":"","content":"I know Stew was planning one. I'm not sure if it'll still happen, but I've pinged him to check. RL often gets in the way of these things, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:48:43-08:00","id":313330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=313312#post313312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there will not be a blog post this week? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There will be, either tomorrow or monday. Lost track of time while getting caught up with some deadlines, I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T19:48:53-08:00","id":313421,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm down for hearing more about character generation and xp costs. We know a fair bit about things so hard to come up with stuff that's not straight up &quot;Just give us entire sections of the book.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, tell us about Protectorates!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T20:35:00-08:00","id":313465,"title":"","content":"I guess I have a few lingering questions, and the comments are closed for the ask anything blog.<br /> <br /> Do Pure have a chosen prey? Do they do the Siskur-Dah? Would the Bale Hounds? Are the shartha full of hate for the Uratha? Or are some willing to deal? What about the big two, azlu and the beshilu? Are the wayward sons, the other changing breeds from the back of the War Against the Pure book still 'canon?' And with the revamped information on Helios, does it have an Uratha analog?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T21:01:15-08:00","id":313472,"title":"","content":"Make those questions in t he blood. He's not gonna be checking the forum when he makes the post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T02:08:10-08:00","id":313573,"title":"","content":"Wha? As Monghani said, <i>comments are closed on the blog post</i>. It's an auto-timeout anti-spam thing. Since I'm posting here, it's logical to think I'd take questions here, and I will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T02:52:13-08:00","id":313587,"title":"","content":"In which case... how is essence farmed/gained?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T09:14:12-08:00","id":313754,"title":"","content":"Narrative/Character-creation question:<br /> the first draft of the Cahalith show us some interesting faces (dreamer, lore keeper and war howler).<br /> Will the elodoth have a more ''physical'' face (like the war howler could be for the cahalith) exept the classic ''diplomat'', or the rahu something more ''social'' or 'mental'' (like the old tactician of signs of the moon) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 11-16-2014, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T05:04:29-08:00","id":314388,"title":"","content":"Answers may take a couple of days, trapped nerve in my shoulder makes itt hard to type much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:55:17-08:00","id":314555,"title":"","content":"Get better soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T12:35:50-08:00","id":320107,"title":"","content":"Question needed for my next game session: <b>Does Uratha natural weapons ( claws and jaws ) makes damage to spirits in material form (Not in Shadow Realm)?</b> Are they automatically can attack spirits in Twilight? Or does they need special ritual for that? What about Claimed? Would it be different if they attack Malejin / Inferno demons-spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:50:04-08:00","id":320830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=320107#post320107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question needed for my next game session: <b>Does Uratha natural weapons ( claws and jaws ) makes damage to spirits in material form (Not in Shadow Realm)?</b> Are they automatically can attack spirits in Twilight? Or does they need special ritual for that? What about Claimed? Would it be different if they attack Malejin / Inferno demons-spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>Does Uratha natural weapons ( claws and jaws ) makes damage to spirits in material form (Not in Shadow Realm)?</i><br /> <br /> All weapons damage spirits that are materialised, including Uratha natural weapons. Uratha that are 2 ranks higher than the spirit in question count as its Bane and deal Aggravated damage to it if it is materialised.<br /> <br /> <i>Are they automatically can attack spirits in Twilight? Or does they need special ritual for that?</i><br /> <br /> While Uratha can detect spirits that are in Twilight easily, they can only attack them directly if the Uratha is the spirit's Bane, ie is 2 ranks higher than it, or is using whatever the spirit's Bane is as a method of attack. In this case, they deal... can't remember immediately off-hand, is it Lethal or Bashing you deal to a Twilight entity via its Bane? If lacking the Bane or the sheer spirit rank to overwhelm the spirit, Uratha need to use the Bone Shadow Sacred Hunt, use a rite to pull the spirit out of Twilight, unleash their own spiritual allies into Twilight to attack it, or some other esoteric method.<br /> <br /> <i>What about Claimed?</i><br /> <br /> Claimed are symbiotic beings made from a creature of flesh and a spirit; Claimed are (usually) materialised and thus can be struck with attacks as per normal. Now, <i>detecting</i> Claimed that haven't gone all body-horror gribbly and that are acting subtly is going to be tricky unless you're a Storm Lord or have Insight Gifts...<br /> <br /> <i>Would it be different if they attack Malejin / Inferno demons-spirits? </i><br /> <br /> Wounded spirits would, I imagine, work the same as the above. Inferno demons, I don't know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:25:19-08:00","id":321027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/297246-werewolf-2e-question-for-developers-writers-and-testers?p=320830#post320830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha that are 2 ranks higher than the spirit in question count as its Bane and deal Aggravated damage to it if it is materialised.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does Uratha spiritual Rank counted? Highest Renown of werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T14:04:11-08:00","id":321049,"title":"","content":"In 1e, there's a table for calculating your Rank based on the sum of all your Renown dots - it's not equivalent to just your highest Renown dots.<br /> <br /> IIRC there's a similar table for it in 2e, but the numbers are different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}